T10:53:25Z","committedDate":"2026-10-05T10:53:25Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:14:16.118Z","repositoryId":1184090452,"sha":"31430f355f2890596e42931bc73bbc24d3aef981"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"BartWaardenburg","providerType":"User"},"email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"authoredDate":"2026-10-05T10:32:38Z","committedDate":"2026-10-05T10:32:38Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:14:16.118Z","repositoryId":1184090452,"sha":"159a0a1df97f6c7786012886912bc912bfc0cecf"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:14:16.118Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/32e0e70b8a306d58d0ffac24eb0c7a32c51d9289/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:28:37Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:28:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: remove false unused findings from jest, Nx, codegen and workspace configs (#3294)\n\n## What\n\nA large Nx monorepo (about 2.5 million lines, 31,000 files) gave thousands of false unused findings. This change removes five causes. Each cause has a regression test, and each is listed in the changelog.\n\n- **Jest configs.** Read `jest-*.config.*` and `jest.*.config.*`. Map a `testRegex` that is only a literal suffix, such as `\\.integration-spec\\.ts$`, to a glob. Let the entry patterns of every jest config add up. Before, one config with its own pattern dropped the default test files of the others. Credit a `--config` file that a script passes to `jest`.\n- **Class members.** A member that a leaf class calls now reaches the base of a long `extends` chain. An access through one child does not reach a sibling.\n- **GraphQL Codegen.** Read `codegen*.{ts,js,cjs,mjs}` and use the `documents` globs as entry points.\n- **Nx `run-commands` targets.** Read the commands of `project.json` targets as scripts, with `{projectRoot}`, `{workspaceRoot}`, `configurations`, and calls to other targets. Inlined text has a byte budget, because a `project.json` is untrusted input. A target that runs from another directory is skipped.\n- **`workspaces.patterns`.** The config key was documented, but no code read it. It now adds workspace packages for analysis, `list`, and `--workspace` in `check`, `dupes` and `health`. `flags`, `security`, `suppressions`, `--group-by package` and `coverage` still read the manifest globs only.\n\nA CI `run:` block with a JavaScript array literal also no longer logs `invalid entry pattern` on every run.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo doc` with `-D warnings` pass.\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib --bins --tests --examples` passes on the merged tree.\n- On the large Nx monorepo, unused files go from 5,440 to 3,595 (1,627 with `workspaces.patterns` set for its app packages). No file became newly unused. Three other real projects give identical results.\n\n## Not in this change\n\nThe TypeORM `DataSource` migration globs, a `twenty-sdk`-style define-call plugin, and exports that sit in files already reported as unused are open and need a design decision.","tree":{"sha":"0126e7dcb7c3eb5ffcfdd8a53ae49f4d9e009fdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/0126e7dcb7c3eb5ffcfdd8a53ae49f4d9e009fdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/32e0e70b8a306d58d0ffac24eb0c7a32c51d9289","verification":{"payload":"tree 0126e7dcb7c3eb5ffcfdd8a53ae49f4d9e009fdc\nparent bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791473317 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791473317 +0200\n\nfix: remove false unused findings from jest, Nx, codegen and workspace configs (#3294)\n\n## What\n\nA large Nx monorepo (about 2.5 million lines, 31,000 files) gave thousands of false unused findings. This change removes five causes. Each cause has a regression test, and each is listed in the changelog.\n\n- **Jest configs.** Read `jest-*.config.*` and `jest.*.config.*`. Map a `testRegex` that is only a literal suffix, such as `\\.integration-spec\\.ts$`, to a glob. Let the entry patterns of every jest config add up. Before, one config with its own pattern dropped the default test files of the others. Credit a `--config` file that a script passes to `jest`.\n- **Class members.** A member that a leaf class calls now reaches the base of a long `extends` chain. An access through one child does not reach a sibling.\n- **GraphQL Codegen.** Read `codegen*.{ts,js,cjs,mjs}` and use the `documents` globs as entry points.\n- **Nx `run-commands` targets.** Read the commands of `project.json` targets as scripts, with `{projectRoot}`, `{workspaceRoot}`, `configurations`, and calls to other targets. Inlined text has a byte budget, because a `project.json` is untrusted input. A target that runs from another directory is skipped.\n- **`workspaces.patterns`.** The config key was documented, but no code read it. It now adds workspace packages for analysis, `list`, and `--workspace` in `check`, `dupes` and `health`. `flags`, `security`, `suppressions`, `--group-by package` and `coverage` still read the manifest globs only.\n\nA CI `run:` block with a JavaScript array literal also no longer logs `invalid entry pattern` on every run.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo doc` with `-D warnings` pass.\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib --bins --tests --examples` passes on the merged tree.\n- On the large Nx monorepo, unused files go from 5,440 to 3,595 (1,627 with `workspaces.patterns` set for its app packages). No file became newly unused. Three other real projects give identical results.\n\n## Not in this change\n\nThe TypeORM `DataSource` migration globs, a `twenty-sdk`-style define-call plugin, and exports that sit in files already reported as unused are open and need a design decision.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx7alCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASm0QACdleKRS3ipMc4hQcEDel6Zv\nxSOvR8NzsP6dUWeJKTMryXfV62J75IIsdD1gIDYy8ZzET87UApHVwMAezD+PTewU\nKf2xRgDDlVgtmWZrmJWFv+XZMN333rzo3I2e2iMmbW2iqwjCQf92QaD7l/BRW0aa\nG616kIrArnl9GXD8PKhVgkStweYHqtcLOWU7zpWgEAHk3Kh/KSmEkwHxgmjRhF5Q\n7Y2LyJXltvnYfEfyeGGdfEErKtmuA1hxhfkRU4YDPbKAlyCs2qEqj6ruucwMxq+c\ny1uWgNn///JFiZVhjDAJs6hYh6DPmFH033H5TZUGQA3bGtU39JtFcnwM6H4ClraS\n2PwAJTUfduxKtGqQ0/gi99ffv02eW9vRLSIvGAIFCNL60kbjLHfLSBSRbx2Q2X4O\nIaqQEMmu45wnunFJ7SU33vKNz5FpJhqr/vAJgHO0Bhq7Z4Uxm/o4LFYPioWUxoTK\nHjKrRKJtkzWIly5U98NDtvHXrn3d59xvNSaE4svLhaOPKty2ffJHjNSgFD6+meUA\ny+dT2B/mLe6LUkv+z2iK/L3Xb9TcMb6OKEMdl5gK+lV58niUgV9IpB1/7KVjLFcG\nlfVVLo+P4MFTe+yxWNLJsoi9x9r9s1i68y6+JsI02A4C3ovGlTJts8PMr3SAXpu9\nbjsLdnl0fEoUAc8Jkjbi\n=r7F/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T15:28:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/32e0e70b8a306d58d0ffac24eb0c7a32c51d9289","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKDMyZTBlNzBiOGEzMDZkNThkMGZmYWMyNGViMGM3YTMyYzUxZDkyODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e","sha":"bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e"}],"sha":"32e0e70b8a306d58d0ffac24eb0c7a32c51d9289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/32e0e70b8a306d58d0ffac24eb0c7a32c51d9289"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:47:41Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:47:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(baselines): add fallow baselines prune (#3295)\n\nA fixed finding leaves its entry in a committed baseline, and a whole-project --fail-on-stale-baseline run then fails until the file is saved again. fallow baselines prune reads the audit.* baseline paths, runs one whole-project analysis and keeps exactly the entries that --baseline matches. It never adds an entry. Files with an older key form are skipped with the command that saves them again.\n\nRefs #3281","tree":{"sha":"bdc80de4f1d79ba9c9a7768f96faaab49896914e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/bdc80de4f1d79ba9c9a7768f96faaab49896914e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e","verification":{"payload":"tree bdc80de4f1d79ba9c9a7768f96faaab49896914e\nparent fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791470861 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791470861 +0200\n\nfeat(baselines): add fallow baselines prune (#3295)\n\nA fixed finding leaves its entry in a committed baseline, and a whole-project --fail-on-stale-baseline run then fails until the file is saved again. fallow baselines prune reads the audit.* baseline paths, runs one whole-project analysis and keeps exactly the entries that --baseline matches. It never adds an entry. Files with an older key form are skipped with the command that saves them again.\n\nRefs #3281","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx60NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx28QAC3QEOnl8PItIfu8HMFhkbiH\nCnne1+Cr3hrfP173+ERwv4i8yb2yf69TMeFXNupE4X4g0tsATCGeu0CvQGGQBFrN\nD5jHU+djdQtOuJS78fuKe7J2kJ1HzlyujnItingx0EJdesC3ZVe5MwH7S2QMqcYg\nmxEHXOxjJpA6LkSFi1gSE4ZdcgG5zrFla07551aH+whYW4h46gYrB6NU9U1zFZBt\ngxLDq7d1Ln7h0APlrzSx2RuziqAZOChPh/jLUgBhjscN2jBuWworHNJ5X+M2m+D3\nG7wTe4csWQ/0/EPpAWQLscQovKfREKiRqCoRvpSaQ0CwuKHjrwr9Sp6LJTbIrddh\nKimVudfRya7UPAdYsBdVekRyITUrvo/VJ3uSLxfsMZv34Bbom9AjtxCSa/z+PAfF\nSSg5Q0caSBBs0Qf8SX1qZyfiec2i9rZ5Ov6pTFlSvVITmd8IwCSxUNG/y462mc16\nFynPy+BRK7VdRAyL6cwRHmTebKxiK70prJ8wiYPOph3XcPegyA38PuU1A3TD9KQu\nfvhn1qQdYQOI1KZb7Rh/wfwuGWiLC19YNErFS3SU4nebMS2Oxw0nTsdzHi8UhZOp\neXbJAxCo/M8eI5P8BQBYgikoy5AEEWMMrNMlwIDmZHvpK41MXgO0ldYBAU6nHXJW\neL9vPkbVSGT04LJBqKBt\n=ob6O\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T14:47:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKGJkYzVkYTkwN2FmNDRiYWZiMGNkOGViMjlkMTE4NzFhNDM5MTNmMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09","sha":"fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09"}],"sha":"bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/bdc5da907af44bafb0cd8eb29d11871a43913f0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:05:57Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:05:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(drift): turn off git auto maintenance in fixture repositories (#3296)\n\nThe drift harness failed on CI with \"unable to create temporary file\" in\n`git add -A` while it built a fixture repository.\n\nGit 2.55 runs `git maintenance run --auto` in the background after\n`git commit`. Its geometric repack starts when two loose objects share the\n`objects/17` sample directory. The base commit of one generated case meets\nthis condition. The background `git repack -d` then removes packed loose\nobjects and empty object directories while the head `git add -A` writes\ninto them. Git 2.56 raised the threshold, so local runs did not show it.\n\nThe fixture `git` helper now sets `maintenance.auto=false` and `gc.auto=0`.\nA new test forces the repack decision and checks that a fixture commit\nwrites no pack.","tree":{"sha":"b70abc25c1cd16380b96d5e39989b5471164a9e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/b70abc25c1cd16380b96d5e39989b5471164a9e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09","verification":{"payload":"tree b70abc25c1cd16380b96d5e39989b5471164a9e6\nparent d98b6789a6d30ddd51347a71916117a2c02a812d\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791468357 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791468357 +0200\n\ntest(drift): turn off git auto maintenance in fixture repositories (#3296)\n\nThe drift harness failed on CI with \"unable to create temporary file\" in\n`git add -A` while it built a fixture repository.\n\nGit 2.55 runs `git maintenance run --auto` in the background after\n`git commit`. Its geometric repack starts when two loose objects share the\n`objects/17` sample directory. The base commit of one generated case meets\nthis condition. The background `git repack -d` then removes packed loose\nobjects and empty object directories while the head `git add -A` writes\ninto them. Git 2.56 raised the threshold, so local runs did not show it.\n\nThe fixture `git` helper now sets `maintenance.auto=false` and `gc.auto=0`.\nA new test forces the repack decision and checks that a fixture commit\nwrites no pack.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx6NGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7wAQAEDMBULX/ESi74wcQkBtwyh3\nMrA1FPgnKHYIfNwb+Vmdqb3/Nlzdc97rPeQqdWzaY4xdgBsO5kqp4ewBUygcMSVP\nW4wylan4EpY40+5hdOUNHtN4zlsDxEym7h7rh+wvAeDO/pin6h/GZohlMp4VtV+X\nKRJYXcywGFefiy9AigfIZhHB9jvc24QbWY4/ijknqS0M2HRqpAB7a9FyXwnUzs1I\nutpLREE7kgLZZxj8O5U/VDkF5iRwuonmeampBPXNzlkpsIBactqU5TixH9IqVd+B\ngdpz+fhwTbJThWpAwUH6kAhaBekQLMWQN8QgsLj86lYPURlEbb9M38OJqrsr5p/U\n5tu535enfAEQIxz94lz/xdw/pf0xxFiNShxSU5PLMDcaXcFQKQ8VZ1PXeAm+3EGz\n+nFIyrbTYHg6YG2ouXjFqq/Cqk9BGQTb33J+jjXHnVPNMYJC9NkAB8Bx7DJKasdt\n1H9kmA/YvV2M0bPVOMb7Pfc5fgTWEanZ96sTbBV54tTMD24rEQsASQW+9nVEbG1T\nYVSwtWmCfNeHICVKQ2oxt2Vdmo0ba+PeCoCr/ApiYJ84JUJHSKU5651kMRfZamfA\nO6nIbIsVj0H0gyeEH5ki2FZIxkhCZ4p0/ngdPhetoTBEd94ghdEMCiZTQGXoi6tU\nG3f603Bc4gOdriWf9HLT\n=8f/v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T14:05:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKGZiYTVjNjlmMmI1NjFjNGE1ZGY0OTM1MTkzNDViNmE3Y2MyYTBjMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/d98b6789a6d30ddd51347a71916117a2c02a812d","sha":"d98b6789a6d30ddd51347a71916117a2c02a812d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/d98b6789a6d30ddd51347a71916117a2c02a812d"}],"sha":"fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/fba5c69f2b561c4a5df493519345b6a7cc2a0c09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/d98b6789a6d30ddd51347a71916117a2c02a812d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:40:33Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:40:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dupes): give unparseable clone fragments their own fingerprint (#3292)\n\nA clone that stops inside a block does not parse on its own, so every such group hashed to the empty token sequence and got a report-order -rN suffix. The baseline then matched groups by order. Fall back to the lexical tokenizer when the parser gives no tokens, and flag baselines that still hold the old shared keys as legacy.\n\nFixes #3290","tree":{"sha":"5c44ebb28328fdf241a4ffd228f639a0387abf47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/5c44ebb28328fdf241a4ffd228f639a0387abf47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/d98b6789a6d30ddd51347a71916117a2c02a812d","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c44ebb28328fdf241a4ffd228f639a0387abf47\nparent a95710c30af5ea044878bec0afb1baa50d736a6c\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791463233 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791463233 +0200\n\nfix(dupes): give unparseable clone fragments their own fingerprint (#3292)\n\nA clone that stops inside a block does not parse on its own, so every such group hashed to the empty token sequence and got a report-order -rN suffix. The baseline then matched groups by order. Fall back to the lexical tokenizer when the parser gives no tokens, and flag baselines that still hold the old shared keys as legacy.\n\nFixes #3290","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx49BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEtcQAAMx3d4u+MBjaS9/XmU7mhHE\n+eOdknQm7c0AnhtR9ake5V+2ywsSMibS6i+8iIs/yIxgvdaBdzvSAZcB6W6ZFVzY\nxC9ynHVybn3ZLd77+YkwBzBvebrYTLDwJsEOiZ3LcRQBgRMKrreFSDYfCKeziNzA\nqrQs0gKMByWnOPH5VyZZ29BdfSqrrcHhLW072ANn9Q+eWtUiIDqT2ElGGAHcd8Dg\nIVgfcql4ivi82ezaihzIMWAkbgqsmYSZ/Ae6Auzw4Y32Jtgf7S8+LLI06WrwqKal\nGYVy7