w/commits/4f6e5f5ccd8ee58ea5d2b4483a883c5153aef30e"}],"sha":"2cda155fb9e284b051c3d646d2ee4fc6a92f1f36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/2cda155fb9e284b051c3d646d2ee4fc6a92f1f36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/4f6e5f5ccd8ee58ea5d2b4483a883c5153aef30e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:58:01Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:58:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: give fallow architecture its own JSON envelope on every surface (#3288)\n\n## Summary\n\n`fallow architecture` (#3275) is not released yet. Before this change, its JSON output was the `dead-code` envelope. This change gives the command its own machine contract on every surface where other analysis commands appear, and adds a table that makes a missing surface fail a test.\n\n- `fallow architecture --format json` writes `kind: \"architecture\"` with its own `schema_version` (1). With `--group-by`, the kind is `architecture-grouped`.\n- The body is the dead-code body. The finding arrays, finding ids, actions, exit codes, `gate_outcomes`, severities and baselines do not change.\n- `fallow dead-code` JSON, bare `fallow` JSON, `fallow --only/--skip architecture` and `fallow audit` JSON are byte-identical to `origin/main`.\n\n## Contract\n\n| Surface | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fallow architecture --format json` | `kind: \"dead-code\"`, `schema_version: 10` | `kind: \"architecture\"`, `schema_version: 1` |\n| `fallow architecture --group-by <mode> --format json` | `kind: \"dead-code-grouped\"` | `kind: \"architecture-grouped\"` |\n| `_meta` with `--explain` | dead-code rules, architecture docs URL | architecture rules only, architecture docs URL |\n| `docs/output-schema.json` and generated TypeScript | no architecture branch | `ArchitectureOutput`, `ArchitectureGroupedOutput`, `ArchitectureSchemaVersion` |\n| `fallow report --from` | rendered it as a `dead-code` envelope | renders `architecture` and `architecture-grouped` in every format |\n| PR comment and review title | \"codebase report\" | \"architecture report\" |\n| `next_steps` `recheck-baseline` | `fallow dead-code --baseline ...` | `fallow architecture --baseline ...` |\n| Regression regenerate hints | `fallow dead-code --save-regression-baseline` | `fallow architecture --save-regression-baseline` |\n| `--save-baseline` file | `kind: \"dead-code\"` | unchanged: `kind: \"dead-code\"` |\n| `fallow_api` | none | `run_architecture`, `serialize_architecture_programmatic_json` |\n| Node bindings | none | `detectArchitecture` returns `ArchitectureReport` |\n| MCP | none | `check_architecture`, Code Mode `checkArchitecture` |\n| `detectCircularDependencies`, `detectBoundaryViolations`, MCP `analyze` | `kind: \"dead-code\"` | unchanged |\n\nThe architecture body is the dead-code body, so a change to that shared body bumps `CHECK_SCHEMA_VERSION` and `ARCHITECTURE_SCHEMA_VERSION` together. `docs/backwards-compatibility.md` states this rule, and a schema test checks that the two definitions keep the same properties.\n\nOther fixes in the same area:\n\n- The typed root enum now has the `trace-error` variant.\n- The schema kind table now lists `similar-code-status` and `similar-code-cache-clear`. Before, a validator that used the schema rejected their valid output.\n- The help text of `--baseline`, `--save-baseline`, `--sarif-file`, `--fail-on-parse-error` and `report --from` names `architecture`. The rejection messages of these flags on other commands name `fallow architecture` too.\n- The MCP baseline warning says \"issue\" for the grouped dead-code and architecture kinds, as it does for the flat kinds.\n- The root README lists `detectArchitecture` with the other Node exports.\n\n## Drift guards\n\n`crates/types/src/command_surfaces.rs` has one row per analysis subcommand with its kinds, its `report --from` status, its MCP tool, its verdict case and its CI integration status. Every other visible subcommand is listed with a reason. Tests read the table:\n\n- Every visible clap subcommand is in exactly one list (`crates/cli/src/lib.rs`).\n- Every row kind is a schema branch, and the typed root enum and the schema kind table have the same kinds (`schema_emit.rs`).\n- The architecture schema definitions keep the dead-code body and describe the architecture command (`schema_emit.rs`).\n- `report --from` renders or refuses each kind as the row says (`cli_report.rs`).\n- Every row MCP tool names `fallow <command>` as its CLI analogue (`command_surfaces.rs`).\n- Every rendered command has a saved-report parity test that runs `fallow <command>` (`report_parity_tests.rs`).\n- The live schema conformance test records each kind that it validates and fails when a row kind has no case (`schema_conformance.rs`).\n- The valid-command lists of the GitHub Action and both copies of the GitLab template, and the job summary routing, equal the routed rows. `flags` and `similar-code` are omitted with a reason (`ci_command_routing_tests.rs`).\n- Every row with a verdict has a drift I7 case (`crates/cli/tests/drift/main.rs`).\n- The root README and the package README name every Node export (`crates/napi/src/lib.rs`).\n\nThe drift harness also changes:\n\n- I14 asserts the root kinds, then compares exit codes, finding keys, finding ids, `gate_outcomes` and the report body, flat and grouped.\n- A new I2 case compares the CLI, `fallow_api::run_architecture` and both paths of MCP `check_architecture`.\n- I7 runs `architecture`, flat and grouped.\n- `docs/development/drift-contract.md` has an \"Add a command\" checklist.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New tests fail on an `origin/main` binary: 10 integration tests, among them the architecture kind tests, the saved-report parity test and the live schema conformance test.\n- [x] Each new guard fails on a broken variant: the README export guard without `detectArchitecture` in the root README, the schema description test with the cloned dead-code description, the conformance test without the `architecture` case, the parity guard with the architecture row pointed at another test, and the CI guard with `architecture` removed from `action/scripts/analyze.sh`.\n- [x] `cargo test -p fallow-cli --lib --test integration --test drift`\n- [x] `cargo test -p fallow-output -p fallow-api -p fallow-mcp -p fallow-types -p fallow-node`\n- [x] `cargo test -p fallow-cli --features schema-emit --bin fallow-schema-emit`\n- [x] `cargo build -p fallow-mcp && cargo test -p fallow-cli --test drift -- --include-ignored`\n- [x] `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- [x] `cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items` with `-D warnings`\n- [x] `bash action/tests/run.sh` with the new binary (the native fastpath renders the architecture fixture)\n- [x] `bash ci/tests/run.sh`\n- [x] `node crates/napi/test.mjs` after `npm run build:debug`\n- [x] `npm run generate:contracts:check`, `npm run check:agent-adapters`, `npm run verify:fast`\n- [x] Byte identity against an `origin/main` binary on `tests/fixtures/boundary-violations`, `tests/fixtures/package-cycle-workspace`, `editors/vscode` and `viz-frontend`: `dead-code`, bare, `--only dead-code`, `dead-code --group-by directory` and `audit` JSON are identical after `elapsed_ms` and `analysis_run_id` are removed. Bare `--only architecture`, `--skip architecture`, and the SARIF, CodeClimate, markdown, compact and GitHub annotation output are identical too. `fallow architecture` differs only in the root `kind` and `schema_version`.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- The public docs repository needs the matching edits on its architecture branch: the JSON example, `report --from`, the MCP tool and the Node binding.\n- `fallow guard --format json` has no root `kind`. The command table lists it with a reason, but the envelope gap stays.\n\n## Related\n\n- User docs: fallow-rs/docs#92. Merge it together with this PR.","tree":{"sha":"58df00e6ff73843e78022f46d605521951e65f2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/58df00e6ff73843e78022f46d605521951e65f2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/4f6e5f5ccd8ee58ea5d2b4483a883c5153aef30e","verification":{"payload":"tree 58df00e6ff73843e78022f46d605521951e65f2c\nparent 933b090d88e9897ad583e503d9df20ca5a3c24a4\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791457081 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791457081 +0200\n\nfeat: give fallow architecture its own JSON envelope on every surface (#3288)\n\n## Summary\n\n`fallow architecture` (#3275) is not released yet. Before this change, its JSON output was the `dead-code` envelope. This change gives the command its own machine contract on every surface where other analysis commands appear, and adds a table that makes a missing surface fail a test.\n\n- `fallow architecture --format json` writes `kind: \"architecture\"` with its own `schema_version` (1). With `--group-by`, the kind is `architecture-grouped`.\n- The body is the dead-code body. The finding arrays, finding ids, actions, exit codes, `gate_outcomes`, severities and baselines do not change.\n- `fallow dead-code` JSON, bare `fallow` JSON, `fallow --only/--skip architecture` and `fallow audit` JSON are byte-identical to `origin/main`.\n\n## Contract\n\n| Surface | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fallow architecture --format json` | `kind: \"dead-code\"`, `schema_version: 10` | `kind: \"architecture\"`, `schema_version: 1` |\n| `fallow architecture --group-by <mode> --format json` | `kind: \"dead-code-grouped\"` | `kind: \"architecture-grouped\"` |\n| `_meta` with `--explain` | dead-code rules, architecture docs URL | architecture rules only, architecture docs URL |\n| `docs/output-schema.json` and generated TypeScript | no architecture branch | `ArchitectureOutput`, `ArchitectureGroupedOutput`, `ArchitectureSchemaVersion` |\n| `fallow report --from` | rendered it as a `dead-code` envelope | renders `architecture` and `architecture-grouped` in every format |\n| PR comment and review title | \"codebase report\" | \"architecture report\" |\n| `next_steps` `recheck-baseline` | `fallow dead-code --baseline ...` | `fallow architecture --baseline ...` |\n| Regression regenerate hints | `fallow dead-code --save-regression-baseline` | `fallow architecture --save-regression-baseline` |\n| `--save-baseline` file | `kind: \"dead-code\"` | unchanged: `kind: \"dead-code\"` |\n| `fallow_api` | none | `run_architecture`, `serialize_architecture_programmatic_json` |\n| Node bindings | none | `detectArchitecture` returns `ArchitectureReport` |\n| MCP | none | `check_architecture`, Code Mode `checkArchitecture` |\n| `detectCircularDependencies`, `detectBoundaryViolations`, MCP `analyze` | `kind: \"dead-code\"` | unchanged |\n\nThe architecture body is the dead-code body, so a change to that shared body bumps `CHECK_SCHEMA_VERSION` and `ARCHITECTURE_SCHEMA_VERSION` together. `docs/backwards-compatibility.md` states this rule, and a schema test checks that the two definitions keep the same properties.\n\nOther fixes in the same area:\n\n- The typed root enum now has the `trace-error` variant.\n- The schema kind table now lists `similar-code-status` and `similar-code-cache-clear`. Before, a validator that used the schema rejected their valid output.\n- The help text of `--baseline`, `--save-baseline`, `--sarif-file`, `--fail-on-parse-error` and `report --from` names `architecture`. The rejection messages of these flags on other commands name `fallow architecture` too.\n- The MCP baseline warning says \"issue\" for the grouped dead-code and architecture kinds, as it does for the flat kinds.\n- The root README lists `detectArchitecture` with the other Node exports.\n\n## Drift guards\n\n`crates/types/src/command_surfaces.rs` has one row per analysis subcommand with its kinds, its `report --from` status, its MCP tool, its verdict case and its CI integration status. Every other visible subcommand is listed with a reason. Tests read the table:\n\n- Every visible clap subcommand is in exactly one list (`crates/cli/src/lib.rs`).\n- Every row kind is a schema branch, and the typed root enum and the schema kind table have the same kinds (`schema_emit.rs`).\n- The architecture schema definitions keep the dead-code body and describe the architecture command (`schema_emit.rs`).\n- `report --from` renders or refuses each kind as the row says (`cli_report.rs`).\n- Every row MCP tool names `fallow <command>` as its CLI analogue (`command_surfaces.rs`).\n- Every rendered command has a saved-report parity test that runs `fallow <command>` (`report_parity_tests.rs`).\n- The live schema conformance test records each kind that it validates and fails when a row kind has no case (`schema_conformance.rs`).\n- The valid-command lists of the GitHub Action and both copies of the GitLab template, and the job summary routing, equal the routed rows. `flags` and `similar-code` are omitted with a reason (`ci_command_routing_tests.rs`).\n- Every row with a verdict has a drift I7 case (`crates/cli/tests/drift/main.rs`).\n- The root README and the package README name every Node export (`crates/napi/src/lib.rs`).\n\nThe drift harness also changes:\n\n- I14 asserts the root kinds, then compares exit codes, finding keys, finding ids, `gate_outcomes` and the report body, flat and grouped.\n- A new I2 case compares the CLI, `fallow_api::run_architecture` and both paths of MCP `check_architecture`.\n- I7 runs `architecture`, flat and grouped.\n- `docs/development/drift-contract.md` has an \"Add a command\" checklist.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New tests fail on an `origin/main` binary: 10 integration tests, among them the architecture kind tests, the saved-report parity test and the live schema conformance test.\n- [x] Each new guard fails on a broken variant: the README export guard without `detectArchitecture` in the root README, the schema description test with the cloned dead-code description, the conformance test without the `architecture` case, the parity guard with the architecture row pointed at another test, and the CI guard with `architecture` removed from `action/scripts/analyze.sh`.\n- [x] `cargo test -p fallow-cli --lib --test integration --test drift`\n- [x] `cargo test -p fallow-output -p fallow-api -p fallow-mcp -p fallow-types -p fallow-node`\n- [x] `cargo test -p fallow-cli --features schema-emit --bin fallow-schema-emit`\n- [x] `cargo build -p fallow-mcp && cargo test -p fallow-cli --test drift -- --include-ignored`\n- [x] `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- [x] `cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items` with `-D warnings`\n- [x] `bash action/tests/run.sh` with the new binary (the native fastpath renders the architecture fixture)\n- [x] `bash ci/tests/run.sh`\n- [x] `node crates/napi/test.mjs` after `npm run build:debug`\n- [x] `npm run generate:contracts:check`, `npm run check:agent-adapters`, `npm run verify:fast`\n- [x] Byte identity against an `origin/main` binary on `tests/fixtures/boundary-violations`, `tests/fixtures/package-cycle-workspace`, `editors/vscode` and `viz-frontend`: `dead-code`, bare, `--only dead-code`, `dead-code --group-by directory` and `audit` JSON are identical after `elapsed_ms` and `analysis_run_id` are removed. Bare `--only architecture`, `--skip architecture`, and the SARIF, CodeClimate, markdown, compact and GitHub annotation output are identical too. `fallow architecture` differs only in the root `kind` and `schema_version`.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- The public docs repository needs the matching edits on its architecture branch: the JSON example, `report --from`, the MCP tool and the Node binding.\n- `fallow guard --format json` has no root `kind`. The command table lists it with a reason, but the envelope gap stays.\n\n## Related\n\n- User docs: fallow-rs/docs#92. Merge it together with this PR.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx3c5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/6YQAKLzyBRG3JacWUD6QxL90oFL\nL6UqD66GQFEpe0uSRo+lCONbjMSO2+kFIg+pZPqbe00rpFeePIYtYrD9rZ5ZE6f5\n+8VsaXKhvxvgJpiGrq4ehp+/EOrf/ZY3J97TyFyApUPreMCqugBFrphfIGKuHVIM\nA2lakwd69+uZntXWQEb7S65cgpELwuucf0LOO0+BHsljOM0znDXmLg2Niy/F71WP\nw2XHImoSVMbVp1LBFAkwjEzbbIDeGrSQKQ6V1Gz9SL5+5f4twjRe3XSfAkQ/nSxX\n67kI/w3ihqbozKRk04ecE/CCUIrOv0FH5c21BsOI/497ekVZk7Yn0msYakr7sI29\nHauX6oITZg0WUo2ro4xWPjlODFTrjKPEGz7gEuhAyF5he/3J5DJvpa+HbewyQC9A\nZHvjQqcE3m7SHUyEVtB30DikzL+TvpgtN3Yz+9IkxQgZb4oI2yEjIio/iqb/hjw/\nPnuz7Q/CpjgGBhke57PJp71b7f324UWBDpui0WCdPewAikaNhhys1qaWxUhhSZPq\n0mj4Dmt5H4gVDQ9RS/xxbIQW6YlTRdByiSPsoiizzusSvPYFq3RfeVaNRmsVoq7d\nvnxEE6Hv3p7aabuepeHb0lKanFtzUgXAHqhrwyNfOn1ZDQP/97WjoIJY6034EwYM\ndfmC2QspL2czxXcgW0F9\n=FiCG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T10:58:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/4f6e5f5ccd8ee58ea5d2b4483a883c5153aef30e","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKDRmNmU1ZjVjY2Q4ZWU1OGVhNWQyYjQ0ODNhODgzYzUxNTNhZWYzMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/933b090d88e9897ad583e503d9df20ca5a3c24a4","sha":"933b090d88e9897ad583e503d9df20ca5a3c24a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/933b090d88e9897ad583e503d9df20ca5a3c24a4"}],"sha":"4f6e5f5ccd8ee58ea5d2b4483a883c5153aef30e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/4f6e5f5ccd8ee58ea5d2b4483a883c5153aef30e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/933b090d88e9897ad583e503d9df20ca5a3c24a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:48:55Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:48:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: bump Rust toolchain to 1.99.0 (#3287)\n\nThe macOS PGO build works on 1.99 again, because the release workflows no\nlonger pass the profile flags to Apple clang (#3286). MSRV stays at 1.96.\n\nChanges for the new Clippy and rustc:\n- `assert_is_empty` is allowed workspace-wide. The `assert_eq!` form it\n  suggests needs `[] as [T; 0]` for most collections.\n- Telemetry uses `AtomicBool::try_update`, because `fetch_update` is\n  deprecated. `try_update` is stable since 1.95, so MSRV 1.96 builds it.\n- Two `clippy::float_cmp` expectations are removed. The lint no longer\n  fires on these compares.","tree":{"sha":"4e8eaf0880332db122ebed4d66eae32d70d8505e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/4e8eaf0880332db122ebed4d66eae32d70d8505e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/933b090d88e9897ad583e503d9df20ca5a3c24a4","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e8eaf0880332db122ebed4d66eae32d70d8505e\nparent 6d5e70430876ea901505f2b093c9d20ef72e213f\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791456535 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791456535 +0200\n\nchore: bump Rust toolchain to 1.99.0 (#3287)\n\nThe macOS PGO build works on 1.99 again, because the release workflows no\nlonger pass the profile flags to Apple clang (#3286). MSRV stays at 1.96.\n\nChanges for the new Clippy and rustc:\n- `assert_is_empty` is allowed workspace-wide. The `assert_eq!` form it\n  suggests needs `[] as [T; 0]` for most collections.\n- Telemetry uses `AtomicBool::try_update`, because `fetch_update` is\n  deprecated. `try_update` is stable since 1.95, so MSRV 1.96 builds it.\n- Two `clippy::float_cmp` expectations are removed. The lint no longer\n  fires on these compares.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx3UXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYygQAAl4tv/sAkh5+haEyzl6WB1s\nQWKc+DiJWEltVxDB0Z9uhIkoem8WWZWWiYB6vgE9Fj8piLBQxHUy+zOu6qi9Mamd\nKHnQl8jBDGBJHqw+ZP7RaUl8Yztx+eARgwYM0k9nCp2w25QBhREjnQC+cb44Voit\nDmO7QdMzeEr8Fu9oJAf5YryDhjecG4beKMysT5yZySijRx0j8Li5YdXwo5QYHend\nDn9wa8JS3qN12GJ4UDpDmLJRnX8LnZ6EY6UMy0LCo60ftcA8BSp2mWd7+WA6kOtm\n4+joSa2Ou077ttEV/Y4hgTUNTj9/8iTzU6o7iiSUgNypWMKT9DLcQ8Auh7LT5wg2\nWCzWJlBx8pZ1OZJ/PAtvCIdaibA7I/g2FCQQwKw7J8YY5siy7CD1/MkwIZXKnsjv\nTagpcHiZoiicnPQR0B/9xpz9hsepkMk3Cbm3tR0B2JrM+PluIMaImq8lZuu5kkgb\n38A1VnZuwp3S9NmxYS2KUqiOaYllDfu9Lz+50dBjJrbCypryDupms4gFLGgc2wId\nDsEXIQl6KhXeO0d28hhbQp38pJ1yX5D5ML03Yb3hiuoan1E/uRfLoKM+uG6hQ8W5\nV5CHDRiaQMXiLdjI4ivGk5k4x4hnkWR/veQ+Md9H95ykaQMfSYvr6vaw+yZLuKIt\nSt1ac10VJhgZpwlKd5eD\n=S956\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T10:48:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/