l":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/a7de13161ac896e4ef1298fd7557dd9db31143c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:16:16Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:16:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: map missing lib/ package entries back to src/ (#3219)\n\n* fix: map missing lib/ package entries back to src/\n\n* fix: map ignored lib/ package entries back to src/\n\nA lib/ build output on disk that .gitignore or ignorePatterns excludes\nis not in the analyzed file set. The entry probe found the file on disk,\nkept the lib/ entry, and the graph then dropped it. The package source\nwas reported as unused.\n\nNow the lib/ target counts as present only when the probed file is in\nthe discovered file set. Entry discovery checks the discovered files,\nand the public API entry set checks the graph. A tracked lib/ file stays\nthe entry.\n\nThe output entry helpers were duplicated in fallow-core and\nfallow-engine. They now live in fallow_graph::resolve::output_entry, and\nboth crates call them.\n\n* fix: check ignored lib/ entries in the core public API set\n\nThe core public API entry set (used by the unused class member check)\nresolved package entries with the disk check. For a lib/ build output\nthat .gitignore or ignorePatterns excludes, the set stayed empty, and\ncore and engine gave different results.\n\nNow core resolves these entries against the module graph, the same as\nthe engine. Both crates find the module of a package entry with the new\nModuleGraph::package_entry_file_id. This replaces two copies of the\ncanonical path lookup.\n\noutput_entry_to_source_path now calls is_discovered only for a lib/\nentry that has a same-stem source file. Other entries do not build the\ndiscovered path index.\n\n* test: skip file system output entry tests under Miri\n\n* test: compile the package entry tests only on unix","tree":{"sha":"0bc4ab433104d1287ab48be322c7faccf38f9126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/0bc4ab433104d1287ab48be322c7faccf38f9126"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/a7de13161ac896e4ef1298fd7557dd9db31143c9","verification":{"payload":"tree 0bc4ab433104d1287ab48be322c7faccf38f9126\nparent 52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791270976 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791270976 +0200\n\nfix: map missing lib/ package entries back to src/ (#3219)\n\n* fix: map missing lib/ package entries back to src/\n\n* fix: map ignored lib/ package entries back to src/\n\nA lib/ build output on disk that .gitignore or ignorePatterns excludes\nis not in the analyzed file set. The entry probe found the file on disk,\nkept the lib/ entry, and the graph then dropped it. The package source\nwas reported as unused.\n\nNow the lib/ target counts as present only when the probed file is in\nthe discovered file set. Entry discovery checks the discovered files,\nand the public API entry set checks the graph. A tracked lib/ file stays\nthe entry.\n\nThe output entry helpers were duplicated in fallow-core and\nfallow-engine. They now live in fallow_graph::resolve::output_entry, and\nboth crates call them.\n\n* fix: check ignored lib/ entries in the core public API set\n\nThe core public API entry set (used by the unused class member check)\nresolved package entries with the disk check. For a lib/ build output\nthat .gitignore or ignorePatterns excludes, the set stayed empty, and\ncore and engine gave different results.\n\nNow core resolves these entries against the module graph, the same as\nthe engine. Both crates find the module of a package entry with the new\nModuleGraph::package_entry_file_id. This replaces two copies of the\ncanonical path lookup.\n\noutput_entry_to_source_path now calls is_discovered only for a lib/\nentry that has a same-stem source file. Other entries do not build the\ndiscovered path index.\n\n* test: skip file system output entry tests under Miri\n\n* test: compile the package entry tests only on unix","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKBACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAycgQABGLQ1ea3koQyZ5hMds632Qt\nozH/IPOelVm3/BAkHTEilsncnijT4HbxrSm+LAT3FIcd28VxcoeRxr+WHTgY5h2P\nA286a+Jj4lSRtoIVTMJpyO9P0G5qCXdhhxit+hbIFkxHLBWN3ao4rFbgLDw3H1M4\n3eBOsksbWb0AxcBdwg4Zr1x+RlPGElZBqFpbJ9nW/TUr8EF6DB+nrk3H4AbjlPAD\n5A4Q3CAbYDhQfwhavILZN3pquc131NZOOcUzoMdPp39OZBNIzNVnsYhgIUIdRGbt\nK6JDK2ki87peRKIkwZqJC1AshB315mqLjS8a72w5Nlb6V9YbOfp7ZcdZips48hwC\nQTNBCKt6PgHH5/i1A5x0u8g5Ucvw8wqlh3Ni4vmLnYdxYLgdOmrYGPXogx70Bp20\nch+JUAYZe3mYyqJ1VeWG1t6FIBa6bk3hqaY4URQzCJXEg9Z7kTyPmaV3EDNEA0jY\nTM1QshFLHxpG121h67bTNpbv/wc7D5LPGodqcz8MmiD2cqCCHGEPq9jzHhn94naQ\nPs67rkxkyLAOwGXd6ndB1UxiZPMtdy+TJZfrRPvN7f+dzj+qsHiJfMp65Dx66S4+\nEiRcISVuw6IZUBxV1HEowNMDWSttJwOYp2DEuY2MCexzS3AY+5FOE8DNBQxFonbV\ntaP4iRPMZ50qlWYaSuj+\n=oaLy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:16:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/a7de13161ac896e4ef1298fd7557dd9db31143c9","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKGE3ZGUxMzE2MWFjODk2ZTRlZjEyOThmZDc1NTdkZDlkYjMxMTQzYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68","sha":"52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68"}],"sha":"a7de13161ac896e4ef1298fd7557dd9db31143c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/a7de13161ac896e4ef1298fd7557dd9db31143c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:11:12Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:11:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(extract): sort unique component escapes with cached keys (#3236)\n\nThe component contract collector recorded one escape for each value\nreference to an imported or component binding, then sorted the list with\na Debug-formatted key that each comparison built again. On files with\nmany references this dominated the new extraction cost.\n\nThe collector now skips an escape that it already recorded, and the sort\nbuilds each key once. The sorted, deduplicated list is the same, so the\nextraction cache stays valid. Cold dead-code runs on the pinned zod,\npreact and vue-core benchmark sources execute 6.6 to 15.9 percent fewer\ninstructions, with identical output.","tree":{"sha":"224c38143039146d5257de4b129e64ff21c6836a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/224c38143039146d5257de4b129e64ff21c6836a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68","verification":{"payload":"tree 224c38143039146d5257de4b129e64ff21c6836a\nparent 807e1525e9341e95fab1b35c775dfc92b4efb1e5\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791267072 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791267072 +0200\n\nperf(extract): sort unique component escapes with cached keys (#3236)\n\nThe component contract collector recorded one escape for each value\nreference to an imported or component binding, then sorted the list with\na Debug-formatted key that each comparison built again. On files with\nmany references this dominated the new extraction cost.\n\nThe collector now skips an escape that it already recorded, and the sort\nbuilds each key once. The sorted, deduplicated list is the same, so the\nextraction cache stays valid. Cold dead-code runs on the pinned zod,\npreact and vue-core benchmark sources execute 6.6 to 15.9 percent fewer\ninstructions, with identical output.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxJEACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg9wQABfyCQDndeYTqGCYsJ6FuW9H\n5OuT7KTH2fVvI91hidolf+DA3lbWwOIbCi8RhnW6YbumKK1uKF0P35KcEXrv71yo\nn/43yZGpPm0nlWN8iBituYNl4BFa9E9DhPWMEfUalOvw6l9LdjygcZadS1t25gJs\nH2sRYfOwlkIaQVqa/rGnYIju6PQ8IwpD2crGIuZGMJgW5ivveSzFcZmDbS2EHeLt\nQD2KlUyYr7A8PGLmFGYsO+7OjzA3GalFJEnB+I0KEKll4qaG8DSkuDIvlX7BN11T\nMZ+pKCi/ueYIpL6ZFl/JaoaRz3YuHeF7EAiHxKuy9m4Q8q4YAH5r0GMlNxLQ223q\nY5NDRAb27EThTUAfZpntH/CUVJSYY/4dcV492a/xxEgWs7EDz7s4ozB4I0rZbj5D\nPnq0/uG/eg4r09UmapXXIIr5tPC9w5wiCDG111NplOHJV7SbtcBIfwTcJLVVgdp5\nj7Q6GMz/KV524JgRZYDnQeEogqFF0+ERBYcfaQJWyrjikOMywWx810izjbfLN3Er\nTSjTTbyZDnuK8UOVpe9pgDvF78a0BSjJo+XDJsZ3EBs6fBl/AnrX2oXzCQH2+qLX\nUm4f7YknqiIE4+fxtmsYt/QDj8If6NWhmNSDMxTLSeYl8gXUdr20lmai55Ht/w0C\n5MKjA3DrIVOCF+zxlHc7\n=kUW9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T06:11:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKDUyY2Q5ODVjNmUxNjBiYjkyMTE4N2FjMTY3Yzg2MWUyMTRiZTBkNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/807e1525e9341e95fab1b35c775dfc92b4efb1e5","sha":"807e1525e9341e95fab1b35c775dfc92b4efb1e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/807e1525e9341e95fab1b35c775dfc92b4efb1e5"}],"sha":"52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/52cd985c6e160bb921187ac167c861e214be0d68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/807e1525e9341e95fab1b35c775dfc92b4efb1e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T05:36:27Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T05:36:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(plugins): read tsdown and tsup JSON configs and package.json keys (#3217)\n\nThe tsdown plugin now matches tsdown.config.json and reads the tsdown key in the root package.json. The tsup plugin now matches tsup.config.{mts,cts,json} and reads the tsup key in the root package.json. Both tools load these config forms, so fallow missed their entry files before.\n\nRefs #3209","tree":{"sha":"268d571fcec7d07864258f0068de9372c5679fc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/268d571fcec7d07864258f0068de9372c5679fc2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/807e1525e9341e95fab1b35c775dfc92b4efb1e5","verification":{"payload":"tree 268d571fcec7d07864258f0068de9372c5679fc2\nparent cc2ba83bcdd00e8d62c7bb1e2f6d5e81b4c90676\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791264987 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791264987 +0200\n\nfix(plugins): read tsdown and tsup JSON configs and package.json keys (#3217)\n\nThe tsdown plugin now matches tsdown.config.json and reads the tsdown key in the root package.json. The tsup plugin now matches tsup.config.{mts,cts,json} and reads the tsup key in the root package.json. Both tools load these config forms, so fallow missed their entry files before.\n\nRefs #3209","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxIjbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv1oQAD7TIplkC0U38/uZ25fqUnPH\nek7ZzG7zGn++KOqB4833E5NEts3bA5AiDsWxFxT9/VNT5T8ZjuWxVBZHTRF4Etwn\nFqpET6ecj3zRIfTVURPv4zerTsn4gM4p2wnhL3Wu/gmdqLewu1rEZRXW4/wX+Wxx\n65+CAxBPPAatjqJBBYBeqCts0auAlYm75ve5lduVQGay27T8EI3uENxwzClR2XoV\nlHpDPYUFd1yXhjgpNv2YbMckhGAb4JNCNMyJH