b942798dc82da83242bce3d90efac27e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/8fffc739dfd4ddfa5adaf704d50ae3204c0bd58f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:18:29Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:18:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): skip peer-only declarations in the ancestor manifest walk (#3228)\n\n## Summary\n\nA nested workspace file can use a package that an ancestor workspace installs. Fallow credits that import to the ancestor declaration. A `peerDependencies` entry on the way stopped this walk, so fallow reported the ancestor declaration as unused.\n\nExample shape:\n\n- `packages/kit` is private and has `build-kit` in `devDependencies`.\n- `packages/kit/lib` is publishable and has `build-kit` only in `peerDependencies`.\n- `packages/kit/lib/cli` is private and imports `build-kit`.\n\nBefore this change, fallow reported `build-kit` in `packages/kit/package.json` as an unused devDependency. The same thing happened when the importing workspace itself listed the package only in `peerDependencies`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`ancestor_satisfying_import` tested the `declared` set of each manifest. That set includes `peerDependencies`. A peer entry alone installs nothing, but the walk treated it as the provider and stopped. The root manifest walk (`workspace_chain_installs`) already tests the `installed` set, so the two walks disagreed.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe ancestor walk now tests `installed` for the owning workspace and for each ancestor. It passes peer-only entries and credits the first ancestor workspace that installs the package. The rule for private workspaces and non-production files does not change.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New unit tests for a peer-only intermediate workspace and a peer-only owning workspace. Both failed before the fix.\n- New integration fixture `workspace-ancestor-peer-only-chain`. Before the fix, fallow reported both `build-kit` and `format-kit` as unused devDependencies of `packages/kit`. After the fix, it reports neither, and no unlisted dependency appears.\n- `cargo test -p fallow-core`, `cargo test -p fallow-cli` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass.\n- Several public monorepos show no change in dead-code findings.","tree":{"sha":"e88282c9b394acde2d50dcaba571a720c47322f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/e88282c9b394acde2d50dcaba571a720c47322f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/8fffc739dfd4ddfa5adaf704d50ae3204c0bd58f","verification":{"payload":"tree e88282c9b394acde2d50dcaba571a720c47322f1\nparent 14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249509 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249509 +0200\n\nfix(deps): skip peer-only declarations in the ancestor manifest walk (#3228)\n\n## Summary\n\nA nested workspace file can use a package that an ancestor workspace installs. Fallow credits that import to the ancestor declaration. A `peerDependencies` entry on the way stopped this walk, so fallow reported the ancestor declaration as unused.\n\nExample shape:\n\n- `packages/kit` is private and has `build-kit` in `devDependencies`.\n- `packages/kit/lib` is publishable and has `build-kit` only in `peerDependencies`.\n- `packages/kit/lib/cli` is private and imports `build-kit`.\n\nBefore this change, fallow reported `build-kit` in `packages/kit/package.json` as an unused devDependency. The same thing happened when the importing workspace itself listed the package only in `peerDependencies`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`ancestor_satisfying_import` tested the `declared` set of each manifest. That set includes `peerDependencies`. A peer entry alone installs nothing, but the walk treated it as the provider and stopped. The root manifest walk (`workspace_chain_installs`) already tests the `installed` set, so the two walks disagreed.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe ancestor walk now tests `installed` for the owning workspace and for each ancestor. It passes peer-only entries and credits the first ancestor workspace that installs the package. The rule for private workspaces and non-production files does not change.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New unit tests for a peer-only intermediate workspace and a peer-only owning workspace. Both failed before the fix.\n- New integration fixture `workspace-ancestor-peer-only-chain`. Before the fix, fallow reported both `build-kit` and `format-kit` as unused devDependencies of `packages/kit`. After the fix, it reports neither, and no unlisted dependency appears.\n- `cargo test -p fallow-core`, `cargo test -p fallow-cli` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass.\n- Several public monorepos show no change in dead-code findings.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxExlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0zoQAAM/r4Nh04Jx52o2e5rbMQwG\nKijo83ZCs3uV7GCo6+IIkxEFP2uHF+wUXh0l7HXioexbC8g0RGGyfiXSjhyKIq0S\nQN4rKtr4RjFd7pusQWtd10rPK3WW7R31TkAyOW+bepaQ4jn2TrDs1LN7rJV+vZJg\nlSZ5AZTfv5zUdeF6Svhf4czyC/x4Q7kwRm0bZD7mf/LHlX23tCX4dv/xtH1CVzMk\nW4cmMGfjvrm5rdimX3ar7MQ7jkjK5ZBIJTRye9fErmYxOGhbJ7nI/mT2anFhoL9i\nCwRr0D70Qz8KVWWK/KSQLONB+NUWvqh3Oyz5DLJuAK9HW97/SRh4k5H7wszZm+HH\njD0Ie/IU21pV/LLXjsaHk5GBfRXlIQvQNNiPTPtdqv8FA7A3x7YGJqWtIxk3Nl5h\nweHun5/mfB4Mm3a1M3fb44N+E64d6LHzp5Rl/rwAay7wE2n81l87roPqn36E/RO7\n0jE6GuQFu5SaivGMe+9IMrubZt4Ny3bgPmv+1O43LtG2ua5uRmVrFPUxunmr+1Pp\nWY2DfrDq55wNVhQk/lBgD5+QUS2xcth+6GZ5zKwy9IhTx6pKcguX4hXnhoEY0nAl\ndDubDuG0XWcjRaQFbhTVbNNazUXN8P8+bDp0rRdky40reC9VNjeh3DzUKXq/3176\njQIJMaBoHR2DE382Z20o\n=MtaB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T01:18:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/8fffc739dfd4ddfa5adaf704d50ae3204c0bd58f","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKDhmZmZjNzM5ZGZkNGRkZmE1YWRhZjcwNGQ1MGFlMzIwNGMwYmQ1OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02","sha":"14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02"}],"sha":"8fffc739dfd4ddfa5adaf704d50ae3204c0bd58f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/8fffc739dfd4ddfa5adaf704d50ae3204c0bd58f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:18:16Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:18:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): credit ts-node and tsx that a tool config loads (#3227)\n\n## Summary\n\n`ts-node` and `tsx` are command-line tools in the tooling catalogue. Such a tool gets credit only from a script, CI or hook reference, from a plugin, or from its own config. A tool config can also load these packages, and fallow did not see that. So fallow reported them as unused devDependencies:\n\n- devDependencies `jest` and `ts-node`, script `\"test\": \"jest\"`, and a `jest.config.ts` file: `ts-node` was unused.\n- devDependencies `mocha` and `tsx`, script `\"test\": \"mocha\"`, and `.mocharc.json` with `{\"require\": \"tsx\"}`: `tsx` was unused.\n- devDependency `nodemon` with its config under the package.json `nodemonConfig` key: `nodemon` was unused.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- The Jest plugin did not credit the loader that Jest needs to read a TypeScript config file.\n- The Mocha plugin did not parse its config, so the `require` and `node-option` entries gave no credit.\n- The nodemon plugin checked only a package.json key named `nodemon`. nodemon reads `nodemonConfig`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Jest: a config file with a `.ts`, `.mts` or `.cts` extension credits `ts-node`. When the file has a `@jest-config-loader` pragma, the plugin credits the package that the pragma names.\n- Mocha: the plugin now parses `.mocharc.{json,jsonc,js,cjs,mjs}` and the package.json `mocha` key. It credits the packages in `require` and the module of each `require=`, `import=`, `loader=` and `experimental-loader=` entry in `node-option`. Local file paths give no credit. A YAML `.mocharc` file stays always used but is not parsed.\n- nodemon: the plugin declares `nodemonConfig` as its package.json config key. The `define_plugin!` arm without `resolve_config` now accepts `package_json_config_key`.\n\nA loader that no config names stays unused.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New integration tests with three fixtures under `tests/fixtures/tool-config-loader-*`. Each fixture also has a loader that nothing loads, and that loader stays reported. The tests failed before the fix and pass after it.\n- New unit tests in the Jest and Mocha plugins for the default loader, the pragma, the options pragma, `node-option` entries and local `require` paths.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core -p fallow-cli`.\n- Public projects with a `jest.config.ts` that uses `ts-node`, and with a `.mocharc.json` that loads `tsx` through `require` or `node-option`: no finding changed, because a `tsconfig.json` already credits these loaders through the TypeScript plugin. With the `tsconfig` files removed, the `node-option` project no longer reports `tsx`, and no other finding changed. In the other two projects, a package.json script that runs `tsc` credits the loader, so the output stays the same.","tree":{"sha":"66fd5a0833d609a46a3b53ee4e099cf820623a04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/66fd5a0833d609a46a3b53ee4e099cf820623a04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02","verification":{"payload":"tree 66fd5a0833d609a46a3b53ee4e099cf820623a04\nparent edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249496 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249496 +0200\n\nfix(deps): credit ts-node and tsx that a tool config loads (#3227)\n\n## Summary\n\n`ts-node` and `tsx` are command-line tools in the tooling catalogue. Such a tool gets credit only from a script, CI or hook reference, from a plugin, or from its own config. A tool config can also load these packages, and fallow did not see that. So fallow reported them as unused devDependencies:\n\n- devDependencies `jest` and `ts-node`, script `\"test\": \"jest\"`, and a `jest.config.ts` file: `ts-node` was unused.\n- devDependencies `mocha` and `tsx`, script `\"test\": \"mocha\"`, and `.mocharc.json` with `{\"require\": \"tsx\"}`: `tsx` was unused.\n- devDependency `nodemon` with its config under the package.json `nodemonConfig` key: `nodemon` was unused.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- The Jest plugin did not credit the loader that Jest needs to read a TypeScript config file.\n- The Mocha plugin did not parse its config, so the `require` and `node-option` entries gave no credit.\n- The nodemon plugin checked only a package.json key named `nodemon`. nodemon reads `nodemonConfig`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Jest: a config file with a `.ts`, `.mts` or `.cts` extension credits `ts-node`. When the file has a `@jest-config-loader` pragma, the plugin credits the package that the pragma names.\n- Mocha: the plugin now parses `.mocharc.{json,jsonc,js,cjs,mjs}` and the package.json `mocha` key. It credits the packages in `require` and the module of each `require=`, `import=`, `loader=` and `experimental-loader=` entry in `node-option`. Local file paths give no credit. A YAML `.mocharc` file stays always used but is not parsed.\n- nodemon: the plugin declares `nodemonConfig` as its package.json config key. The `define_plugin!` arm without `resolve_config` now accepts `package_json_config_key`.\n\nA loader that no config names stays unused.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New integration tests with three fixtures under `tests/fixtures/tool-config-loader-*`. Each fixture also has a loader that nothing loads, and that loader stays reported. The tests failed before the fix and pass after it.\n- New unit tests in the Jest and Mocha plugins for the default loader, the pragma, the options pragma, `node-option` entries and local `require` paths.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core -p fallow-cli`.\n- Public projects with a `jest.config.ts` that uses `ts-node`, and with a `.mocharc.json` that loads `tsx` through `require` or `node-option`: no finding changed, because a `tsconfig.json` already credits these loaders through the TypeScript plugin. With the `tsconfig` files removed, the `node-option` project no longer reports `tsx`, and no other finding changed. In the other two projects, a package.json script that runs `tsc` credits the loader, so the output stays the same.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxExYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1usQAKFxqcchWHQ3a6sVEF6r5ke+\nzUIB31DWTNYhzbK+dXRjvei+AJDgoxFtvU5azIUMa3NIKIJYAz88cMlqOaiuvo1i\nYi4no568+V4+UmdUWLn0PZZDSKPFtUjq1SE/AsA4CtPrEQ1t6s+tMVTrWMvSIPfo\nISsC+K4JF665YYWNwnVWDcVV27S5r/ZoVDQ5779PnnU4DgR3p6JFB7+nCPznlvUr\n+1QMkUnQSySOYxoRd6MInYDEtUO8fAzepWKNru3/UoNt8k+XmA+uN3ZcaSG0DhbM\nOvhvXaUcGMbXR1cU36maBYde45BNQ1xEyJxzppwdFS3byuQFUSvTJG5guhN1CHzt\nOZiKDjeaU+xb4uJ8TkRD/pbonWU7QMSO2z0KjFq036FZJc5FY3d/wQtnCCA5t54/\nXn7SGFrhtC2GIckfJ2CQWBa9rx9HckBhlc5IS5ZRlx2ynj04C1EarBF2ds4vX3lB\nouH6g/lXg2MloP3qvT+W0TKENm2gLVTi7EJtoBmpJ8W4MF06UZdkEHbAmiIAGAXf\nkL7rqF3sw4AN+8Qs59EvBtryGt9+CxnzgxUkXk5bKgPVKp5lxbrQfiWE28/FIE9/\nOQep5qCRNLEZgSb9F9LtZZp+lyM42amUFhF6rwGsbZ5KC+Zs1P04CFRFpUpn/Ve0\nMyz2yZO2TUsOMY1Wu0Wt\n=UsxN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T01:18:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKDE0NTA4MjI3ZTk3ODRkNDIyNTMyOWY5YWMwZTY1YmViMGMyMjFjMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc","sha":"edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc"}],"sha":"14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/14508227e9784d4225329f9ac0e65beb0c221c02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:18:03Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:18:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(plugins): read every defineConfig argument and the default testDir in the Playwright plugin (#3226)\n\n## Summary\n\n- The Playwright plugin now reads every argument of `defineConfig(a, b, ...)`. The last argument that sets `testDir` or `testMatch` wins, as in Playwright.\n- An argument that does not resolve to a local object (an imported base config, a spread, a nested merge call) makes `testDir` or `testMatch` dynamic. The plugin then keeps every script below `testDir`, or the conventional test directories.\n- A static `testMatch` without `testDir` now applies below the config directory. Playwright uses the config directory as the default `testDir`.\n- Only the Playwright plugin adds the test entries of all its configs together. The other plugins that replace their default entries (for example Vitest and Jest) keep the entries of the last config again.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- `test_entry_patterns` read the one object that `find_config_object` returns. For `defineConfig(base, { testDir: ''./e2e'' })` with an imported `base`, that is the second object. Fallow did not see the `testMatch` of `base`, so it kept only spec and test file names below `e2e/`. For `defineConfig({ testDir: ''./a'' }, { testDir: ''./e2e'', ... })`, fallow read `./a`. In both cases the real test file and its helpers became unused files.\n- A scope without `testDir` always gave the conventional directories, so a static `testMatch` in that scope had no effect.\n- The registry kept the entries of every replacing config for every plugin. This was correct only for Playwright, and the CHANGELOG described it only for Playwright. For Vitest, a `vite.config.ts` test include stayed an entry next to the include of `vitest.config.ts`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `config_parser::find_config_merge_arguments` returns the resolved arguments of an exported config call with more than one argument.\n- The Playwright plugin folds `testDir` and `testMatch` over these arguments with last-wins semantics. Playwright merges `projects` by name, so `projects` is static only when one argument gives them.\n- A scope with no `testDir` and a static `testMatch` uses the config directory. The conventional directories stay as a fallback.\n- A new `PluginResult` flag, `accumulate_config_entry_patterns`, selects the accumulate behavior. Only the Playwright plugin sets it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New integration fixtures: `playwright-define-config-imported-base`, `playwright-define-config-two-objects`, `playwright-test-match-without-test-dir`. All three tests failed before the fix and pass after it.\n- New unit tests for the merge rules, the config directory default, and the registry last-config-wins behavior.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass.\n- Public projects with Playwright configs, including one that uses `defineConfig(baseConfig, { ... })` with an imported base: `dead-code` output is the same before and after the fix.","tree":{"sha":"1292b88073c8c01375000ca9bebc694ca067ba57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/1292b88073c8c01375000ca9bebc694ca067ba57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 1292b88073c8c01375000ca9bebc694ca067ba57\nparent 1a7b0dde9bf6524dd1a5bc0c6cc445041d57e3da\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249483 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249483 +0200\n\nfix(plugins): read every defineConfig argument and the default testDir in the Playwright plugin (#3226)\n\n## Summary\n\n- The Playwright plugin now reads every argument of `defineConfig(a, b, ...)`. The last argument that sets `testDir` or `testMatch` wins, as in Playwright.\n- An argument that does not resolve to a local object (an imported base config, a spread, a nested merge call) makes `testDir` or `testMatch` dynamic. The plugin then keeps every script below `testDir`, or the conventional test directories.\n- A static `testMatch` without `testDir` now applies below the config directory. Playwright uses the config directory as the default `testDir`.\n- Only the Playwright plugin adds the test entries of all its configs together. The other plugins that replace their default entries (for example Vitest and Jest) keep the entries of the last config again.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- `test_entry_patterns` read the one object that `find_config_object` returns. For `defineConfig(base, { testDir: ''./e2e'' })` with an imported `base`, that is the second object. Fallow did not see the `testMatch` of `base`, so it kept only spec and test file names below `e2e/`. For `defineConfig({ testDir: ''./a'' }, { testDir: ''./e2e'', ... })`, fallow read `./a`. In both cases the real test file and its helpers became unused files.\n- A scope without `testDir` always gave the conventional directories, so a static `testMatch` in that scope had no effect.\n- The registry kept the entries of every replacing config for every plugin. This was correct only for Playwright, and the CHANGELOG described it only for Playwright. For Vitest, a `vite.config.ts` test include stayed an entry next to the include of `vitest.config.ts`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `config_parser::find_config_merge_arguments` returns the resolved arguments of an exported config call with more than one argument.\n- The Playwright plugin folds `testDir` and `testMatch` over these arguments with last-wins semantics. Playwright merges `projects` by name, so `projects` is static only when one argument gives them.\n- A scope with no `testDir` and a static `testMatch` uses the config directory. The conventional directories stay as a fallback.\n- A new `PluginResult` flag, `accumulate_config_entry_patterns`, selects the accumulate behavior. Only the Playwright plugin sets it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New integration fixtures: `playwright-define-config-imported-base`, `playwright-define-config-two-objects`, `playwright-test-match-without-test-dir`. All three tests failed before the fix and pass after it.\n- New unit tests for the merge rules, the config directory default, and the registry last-config-wins behavior.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass.\n- Public projects with Playwright configs, including one that uses `defineConfig(baseConfig, { ... })` with an imported base: `dead-code` output is the same before and after the fix.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxExLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjGoQAH/zt3iPFoLEwtrh00v8XmB1\nmu8Jl2i2cQrEaeMXToAxnsApbX7r3IIci0lrSbZ9rbzVq3afx7UfGKwTUsE5v4Uj\ngEXqEhrw9LkSjeNNDGQ/E7TTo3EwIsTWFeAzfzb+cjU1HoIOdp26sdxtdC5e4L+b\nQijY3jX+EO6SLt/I1wSa5ieiWkIUn5l79LYDPMQAEVrIXxg8JjI3Lfur2K6RsGa3\nCIlBAVS2Q/Vka68XQuxaUlEs/SdQ9/zSIcaA3OVhOUxdcuLMRy5aBHF8x+B/s33n\n7M4B3mDZl6vVQxl6cHrT9a7BaxQTO5K058f4JtDOWapR17I7MLVwC3Mqu0smKo+K\n7845GmEWo7c6BWLDYnOuw8qKCO7ylbapwWs3dJhfw+yVt7sfyrU7Br583dDyNMk7\n9pFWfR/EMvRRZxzAs3R/+Z/ImvcbhuyothCUcTMiUMUctZf4/dK0Pqmgwvo8AZ4+\ny0DRVbkSLkLYAW8vnd2Lzvs6gUu0BsF1HieTjkLNjjWyauOaHJy9uD4MLjzu632g\n5sLgRYEVbslQuf9s7u9nTtJmIDYASivMuldDnLItsQwmhvAYrlqfe7Z6JwXXafum\nY6JZbxaMuBx2kr6E9yga+gmgb+ZDwXX3Dc7D8ldu/ShVMTw28Kfs0zqO4lZumlYq\nZDo5wa8lfsBDMXBZpJVQ\n=BDFj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T01:18:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKGVkZDVkMDc2ZTg1ZTc2MmFmNDM1ZmE4ZWY4ODUwYjE2NjJkMTkzYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/1a7b0dde9bf6524dd1a5bc0c6cc445041d57e3da","sha":"1a7b0dde9bf6524dd1a5bc0c6cc445041d57e3da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/1a7b0dde9bf6524dd1a5bc0c6cc445041d57e3da"}],"sha":"edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/edd5d076e85e762af435fa8ef8850b1662d193bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/1a7b0dde9bf6524dd1a5bc0c6cc445041d57e3da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:49Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): count a tool config in a workspace as evidence for a root tool (#3225)\n\n## Summary\n\nA root manifest can declare a tool such as `karma`, `c8` or `prettier` while the config file of the tool is only in a workspace package. Fallow reported such a tool as an unused devDependency. Now a config file in a workspace package credits the root devDependency.\n\n## Root cause\n\nA plugin credits its tooling devDependencies only when it finds evidence of use, for example a config file of its own. The root plugin run probed the config patterns at the project root only. The workspace plugin run does not activate the plugin when the workspace package does not declare the tool. Thus no run found the config file in `packages/app/`. Plugin config discovery already probes the workspace directories, so `karma.conf.js` was not an unused file, but the tool was an unused devDependency.\n\n## Fix\n\n`record_plugin_tooling` gets a new `extra_roots` input. The root run passes the plugin config search roots, which are the same directories that plugin config discovery uses. Fallow probes the package root first, as before. Only when no config file is there, fallow probes the other directories. The workspace run is not changed.\n\nA large monorepo can have thousands of search roots, so the probe of the extra roots does not read the disk for each (plugin, root, pattern):\n\n- Each pattern resolves against the in-memory candidate index of the discovery walk, the same index that plugin config discovery uses. Each pattern is compiled once, not once per root.\n- The walk also captures the literal always-used file names of a plugin with tooling dependencies, such as `.c8rc.json`, so the index can answer for them.\n- The filesystem probe stays only for a pattern under a directory that the walk does not enter, such as `.husky/**/*`. One `is_dir` check on that directory skips a root before the glob runs.\n- Production mode turns the unused devDependency check off, so it skips the extra roots.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New integration test `plugin_tooling_root_dev_dependency_credited_by_workspace_config` with the fixture `tests/fixtures/plugin-tooling-workspace-config`. The root declares `c8`, `karma`, `nyc` and `prettier`. `packages/app` has `.c8rc.json`, `.prettierrc` and `karma.conf.js`. Before the fix the test reported `c8`, `karma`, `nyc` and `prettier`. After the fix it reports only `nyc`, which has no config file and no reference.\n- `--trace-dependency karma` now shows `tooling_credit` with `packages/app/karma.conf.js`.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass. No snapshot changed.\n- The `dead-code` JSON output on three public monorepos did not change. The run time did not change in a measurable way.\n- Unit tests cover the index path, the disk path without an index, and the disk path for a directory that the walk does not enter.\n- Timing on a generated monorepo with 200 packages and about 6400 directories, optimized build, `plugins_ms` from `--performance`. A first version of this fix probed the disk for each extra root and took about 4.8 s (6.5 s in production mode). With the index, the run takes about 0.85 s against 0.6 s on `main` (1.26 s against 1.09 s in production mode). The machine had a high load during the runs, so the numbers have noise. The `dead-code` JSON output is the same for all three builds.","tree":{"sha":"426191802ae667f43e67e08b81a266083cd7a808","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/426191802ae667f43e67e08b81a266083cd7a808"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/1a7b0dde9bf6524dd1a5bc0c6cc445041d57e3da","verification":{"payload":"tree 426191802ae667f43e67e08b81a266083cd7a808\nparent ce9471fc344083c603126faf2e748d4d7a00ab11\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249469 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249469 +0200\n\nfix(deps): count a tool config in a workspace as evidence for a root tool (#3225)\n\n## Summary\n\nA root manifest can declare a tool such as `karma`, `c8` or `prettier` while the config file of the tool is only in a workspace package. Fallow reported such a tool as an unused devDependency. Now a config file in a workspace package credits the root devDependency.\n\n## Root cause\n\nA plugin credits its tooling devDependencies only when it finds evidence of use, for example a config file of its own. The root plugin run probed the config patterns at the project root only. The workspace plugin run does not activate the plugin when the workspace package does not declare the tool. Thus no run found the config file in `packages/app/`. Plugin config discovery already probes the workspace directories, so `karma.conf.js` was not an unused file, but the tool was an unused devDependency.\n\n## Fix\n\n`record_plugin_tooling` gets a new `extra_roots` input. The root run passes the plugin config search roots, which are the same directories that plugin config discovery uses. Fallow probes the package root first, as before. Only when no config file is there, fallow probes the other directories. The workspace run is not changed.\n\nA large monorepo can have thousands of search roots, so the probe of the extra roots does not read the disk for each (plugin, root, pattern):\n\n- Each pattern resolves against the in-memory candidate index of the discovery walk, the same index that plugin config discovery uses. Each pattern is compiled once, not once per root.\n- The walk also captures the literal always-used file names of a plugin with tooling dependencies, such as `.c8rc.json`, so the index can answer for them.\n- The filesystem probe stays only for a pattern under a directory that the walk does not enter, such as `.husky/**/*`. One `is_dir` check on that directory skips a root before the glob runs.\n- Production mode turns the unused devDependency check off, so it skips the extra roots.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New integration test `plugin_tooling_root_dev_dependency_credited_by_workspace_config` with the fixture `tests/fixtures/plugin-tooling-workspace-config`. The root declares `c8`, `karma`, `nyc` and `prettier`. `packages/app` has `.c8rc.json`, `.prettierrc` and `karma.conf.js`. Before the fix the test reported `c8`, `karma`, `nyc` and `prettier`. After the fix it reports only `nyc`, which has no config file and no reference.\n- `--trace-dependency karma` now shows `tooling_credit` with `packages/app/karma.conf.js`.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass. No snapshot changed.\n- The `dead-code` JSON output on three public monorepos did not change. The run time did not change in a measurable way.\n- Unit tests cover the index path, the disk path without an index, and the disk path for a directory that the walk does not enter.\n- Timing on a generated monorepo with 200 packages and about 6400 directories, optimized build, `plugins_ms` from `--performance`. A first version of this fix probed the disk for each extra root and took about 4.8 s (6.5 s in production mode). With the index, the run takes about 0.85 s against 0.6 s on `main` (1.26 s against 1.09 s in production mode). The machine had a high load during the runs, so the numbers have noise. The `dead-code` JSON output is the same for all three builds.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEw9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaZsQAHGCvzxUGHiDkDNrbOHELDLD\ndwbpqiQiOA8b+zyY/cU2PzcMZ4k/demtKeg1YXmr2C2GkGaa9iWT3eKF5/dJgv2/\neMgjSxl2taKVf2bL/RCOTD9Wb2leRRFPEbZqfI+w4A+EcQqG+R2iXCmQYZqBKS3B\ncVO/PK+Xr4H2DjaZ/2axRvzOqMpWXl1h6WjgPF4ceIEHH0Gn+GSAi7Pb03I3no8S\nEXp2gDH/oi0/B5pMHcujsf14mbkWOxMitejVLFTp87QUaWJ5L/xemj+HXv9IWUB5\nK6Smfm/BQBqEsAxFgk6rckCFCph5qSYBzfC2Jb7qDFh1Ef3a99VkD1ztzlQfrBhb\n787FLwQsXWpZ5mItDUltCla3iE6rQqe