ubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/ce9471fc344083c603126faf2e748d4d7a00ab11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:35Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(output): show the workspaces that declare and import a root dependency (#3224)\n\n## Summary\n\nA root dependency is unused when every import of it uses the declaration in a nearer workspace `package.json`. The finding for this case said only \"never imported\". `--trace-dependency` showed an import of the same package, so users read the finding as a false positive.\n\nNow the finding names the workspaces that declare the package and import it:\n\n```\nlodash (package.json; declared and imported in packages/app)\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`collect_root_unused_categories` gave every root finding an empty workspace context. The workspace pass fills `used_in_workspaces` for a workspace finding, but the root pass had no data about the nearer manifests that the imports use.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Add the additive field `declared_and_imported_in` on `UnusedDependency`. Serde skips the field when it is empty.\n- Build a new index in the unused-dependency pass. For each import, the index records the nearest workspace in the chain of the importer that installs the package. This is the same rule that decides whether the root declaration gets credit.\n- Only a root finding fills the new field. A workspace finding keeps its context in `used_in_workspaces`.\n- The human output, SARIF, GitHub annotations and the GitHub summary show the new context.\n- The human label never shortens the root `package.json`. When the line has no room for the clause, the root finding renders bare, as before.\n- `remove-dependency` stays auto-fixable: the workspace declarations keep the package installed. The `used_in_workspaces` field and the move action do not change.\n- The output schema and the generated contract types include the new field.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New core integration test on the `root-dependency-nearest-manifest-credit` fixture. It failed before the fix (the field was empty) and passes now. It also checks a nested workspace import that uses an ancestor workspace declaration, and that a workspace finding leaves the new field empty.\n- New unit and integration tests for the human label, SARIF, GitHub annotations and the GitHub summary. Each failed before the renderer change.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` on the touched crates, `cargo test` on `fallow-types`, `fallow-core`, `fallow-output`, `fallow-api`, `fallow-lsp`, `fallow-engine` and `fallow-cli`: pass.\n- `npm run generate:contracts:check` and `npm run check:agent-adapters`: pass.\n- Public project check: on a public monorepo, two root devDependencies now carry the workspaces that declare and import them. All other JSON output is identical before and after the change.","tree":{"sha":"820a0d466ab94ceefa35ab2d4cdb5a9206847b95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/820a0d466ab94ceefa35ab2d4cdb5a9206847b95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/ce9471fc344083c603126faf2e748d4d7a00ab11","verification":{"payload":"tree 820a0d466ab94ceefa35ab2d4cdb5a9206847b95\nparent 257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249455 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249455 +0200\n\nfix(output): show the workspaces that declare and import a root dependency (#3224)\n\n## Summary\n\nA root dependency is unused when every import of it uses the declaration in a nearer workspace `package.json`. The finding for this case said only \"never imported\". `--trace-dependency` showed an import of the same package, so users read the finding as a false positive.\n\nNow the finding names the workspaces that declare the package and import it:\n\n```\nlodash (package.json; declared and imported in packages/app)\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`collect_root_unused_categories` gave every root finding an empty workspace context. The workspace pass fills `used_in_workspaces` for a workspace finding, but the root pass had no data about the nearer manifests that the imports use.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Add the additive field `declared_and_imported_in` on `UnusedDependency`. Serde skips the field when it is empty.\n- Build a new index in the unused-dependency pass. For each import, the index records the nearest workspace in the chain of the importer that installs the package. This is the same rule that decides whether the root declaration gets credit.\n- Only a root finding fills the new field. A workspace finding keeps its context in `used_in_workspaces`.\n- The human output, SARIF, GitHub annotations and the GitHub summary show the new context.\n- The human label never shortens the root `package.json`. When the line has no room for the clause, the root finding renders bare, as before.\n- `remove-dependency` stays auto-fixable: the workspace declarations keep the package installed. The `used_in_workspaces` field and the move action do not change.\n- The output schema and the generated contract types include the new field.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New core integration test on the `root-dependency-nearest-manifest-credit` fixture. It failed before the fix (the field was empty) and passes now. It also checks a nested workspace import that uses an ancestor workspace declaration, and that a workspace finding leaves the new field empty.\n- New unit and integration tests for the human label, SARIF, GitHub annotations and the GitHub summary. Each failed before the renderer change.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` on the touched crates, `cargo test` on `fallow-types`, `fallow-core`, `fallow-output`, `fallow-api`, `fallow-lsp`, `fallow-engine` and `fallow-cli`: pass.\n- `npm run generate:contracts:check` and `npm run check:agent-adapters`: pass.\n- Public project check: on a public monorepo, two root devDependencies now carry the workspaces that declare and import them. All other JSON output is identical before and after the change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEwvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVKMQAGf6H4aB5jg8XduKYSFxAQDp\nI88NkybrRqG9pkwAw9hx1F7pC7r0ZsZyCViM1lSDgpsPihX0X0mmbD99jcBP1/Ki\nmzPdW5Vlz79al03ONzlmpe9XmWYzcnHDEt2PHnmjEe/R2SIqd/Kg1jDolig+E1FK\n2D5NYML3qSxiQ/egq7j8vcOl5RFh2zx7QpIC0kV+cFvVlP0lnrZRsDgrx0fv9lrQ\na/oEwkNOMFaITpn4kXktEMN++CQrKefYtN79FcEVi6bAKLJKyrxjvtbDsYpUGBqV\nf4hlCS9+Mo5vWNDkaLlUi0oxKlyGHG2zOvHRrH2O6gdPd8gW+b1QLf6vpd+zZUyr\nalKoJ8jOD0VNlcMHDfsNbzdmKgrURvLUm9BwtEXcH0kgmILNeI32rXxVVHH787aq\ntyg+1tpmz38Uubz6CGmLorQvohTu6LSCrEoMq3EDchHEBwBUw4+/kNDSy9/Hk3qH\n5LK613Nv2/8KIFyTvogiBUNWR86KTz0jRFzMwe28uyGkPDElZQJGmmmD3Owdwosd\nEGLM7zzVNQtYMzAquip84igSAhqhFlPVLxyv4xDJ4rGt5N30TB70wQ9FdmrVr6rE\n8jyANGF4msBI3lDbTBXcDa4cQ13O9uDidLttIDkZ0TMO/trtrorpUJoVu2+Juv2h\ng6PZbmyOIDy/pA0+KS+0\n=zqQU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T01:17:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/ce9471fc344083c603126faf2e748d4d7a00ab11","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKGNlOTQ3MWZjMzQ0MDgzYzYwMzEyNmZhZjJlNzQ4ZDRkN2EwMGFiMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36","sha":"257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36"}],"sha":"ce9471fc344083c603126faf2e748d4d7a00ab11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/ce9471fc344083c603126faf2e748d4d7a00ab11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:21Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(trace): give --trace-dependency the same credits as the dependency report (#3223)\n\n## Summary\n\n`--trace-dependency` (CLI, programmatic API and MCP `trace_dependency`) now gives the same credits as the unused-dependency report. The report reads each declaring manifest on its own. The trace read the project as one unit, so the two disagreed in workspaces:\n\n- A config file or a `package.json` key in a sibling workspace credited a command-line tool that another manifest declares. The trace said `is_used: true`, and the report flagged the dependency.\n- A devDependency that the same manifest lists in `peerDependencies` is not reported. The trace said `UNUSED`.\n- A host that only a workspace installs, in its own `node_modules`, credits its optional peer in that workspace. The trace looked up hosts only from the project root and said `UNUSED`.\n- An import credits only the nearest manifest that installs the package. A root declaration can be flagged while a workspace imports the package. The trace said `USED` and gave no note.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe trace computed its credits from name-level data: every manifest for the catalogue credit, one peer closure from the project root, and no own-peer credit. The detector computes each credit per declaring manifest.\n\n## Fix\n\n- The catalogue credit and the detector now share one helper, `cli_tool_own_config`. The trace checks only the manifests that declare the name in `devDependencies`, and probes only the declaring package root and the project root.\n- The trace gives a new `own-peer` credit, with the manifest path in `config`, when the same manifest lists the devDependency in `peerDependencies`.\n- `peer_dependency_hosts` now runs the root closure and one closure per workspace, seeded with the packages that the workspace imports, as the detector does. `trace_dependency` takes the workspace roots.\n- A new `unused_in` field lists each manifest that the report flags for the name. The human trace prints it as `Reported unused in:`. The field is additive and absent when no manifest is flagged.\n- The JSON schema, the generated TypeScript contracts and the MCP tool description are updated.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New regression tests in `trace_tooling_credit_tests.rs` and `peer_dependency_credit_tests.rs`, with two new fixtures (`catalogue-cli-credit-workspaces`, `optional-peer-in-workspace-install`) and two existing fixtures. The tests failed before the fix and pass after it.\n- `the_trace_agrees_with_the_report_for_every_dev_dependency` now also covers the own-peer fixture.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` and `cargo test` for `fallow-types`, `fallow-core`, `fallow-engine`, `fallow-api`, `fallow-mcp` and `fallow-cli` pass.\n- `npm run generate:contracts:check` and `npm run check:agent-adapters` pass.\n- On real monorepos, the `dead-code` report is unchanged. The trace keeps `is_used`, `peer_of` and `tooling_credit` for the checked names, and adds `unused_in` that matches the report.","tree":{"sha":"5d388044200fe1fea8708aca24da5f80ea5bef4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/5d388044200fe1fea8708aca24da5f80ea5bef4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d388044200fe1fea8708aca24da5f80ea5bef4a\nparent b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249441 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249441 +0200\n\nfix(trace): give --trace-dependency the same credits as the dependency report (#3223)\n\n## Summary\n\n`--trace-dependency` (CLI, programmatic API and MCP `trace_dependency`) now gives the same credits as the unused-dependency report. The report reads each declaring manifest on its own. The trace read the project as one unit, so the two disagreed in workspaces:\n\n- A config file or a `package.json` key in a sibling workspace credited a command-line tool that another manifest declares. The trace said `is_used: true`, and the report flagged the dependency.\n- A devDependency that the same manifest lists in `peerDependencies` is not reported. The trace said `UNUSED`.\n- A host that only a workspace installs, in its own `node_modules`, credits its optional peer in that workspace. The trace looked up hosts only from the project root and said `UNUSED`.\n- An import credits only the nearest manifest that installs the package. A root declaration can be flagged while a workspace imports the package. The trace said `USED` and gave no note.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe trace computed its credits from name-level data: every manifest for the catalogue credit, one peer closure from the project root, and no own-peer credit. The detector computes each credit per declaring manifest.\n\n## Fix\n\n- The catalogue credit and the detector now share one helper, `cli_tool_own_config`. The trace checks only the manifests that declare the name in `devDependencies`, and probes only the declaring package root and the project root.\n- The trace gives a new `own-peer` credit, with the manifest path in `config`, when the same manifest lists the devDependency in `peerDependencies`.\n- `peer_dependency_hosts` now runs the root closure and one closure per workspace, seeded with the packages that the workspace imports, as the detector does. `trace_dependency` takes the workspace roots.\n- A new `unused_in` field lists each manifest that the report flags for the name. The human trace prints it as `Reported unused in:`. The field is additive and absent when no manifest is flagged.\n- The JSON schema, the generated TypeScript contracts and the MCP tool description are updated.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New regression tests in `trace_tooling_credit_tests.rs` and `peer_dependency_credit_tests.rs`, with two new fixtures (`catalogue-cli-credit-workspaces`, `optional-peer-in-workspace-install`) and two existing fixtures. The tests failed before the fix and pass after it.\n- `the_trace_agrees_with_the_report_for_every_dev_dependency` now also covers the own-peer fixture.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` and `cargo test` for `fallow-types`, `fallow-core`, `fallow-engine`, `fallow-api`, `fallow-mcp` and `fallow-cli` pass.\n- `npm run generate:contracts:check` and `npm run check:agent-adapters` pass.\n- On real monorepos, the `dead-code` report is unchanged. The trace keeps `is_used`, `peer_of` and `tooling_credit` for the checked names, and adds `unused_in` that matches the report.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEwhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsL0QAKYQUpCpEOPJGTyuWTKtl2OH\nF1QKAgoQ47zplgN3MNvRGkN4hP0mw9QFvV63wUJ5TgZJhDJLpnYHX3BKJRR8EYac\nuRPMZoDWWAD0b813kJtrSRnn6rE52K+8nBXMlc0//m2BpSQY+Ys2mNP53FtqZHXS\nskwVwlH+C9F34UJbCjp6bz+wspBJoUawT4FJQg2T4k6oF+eoOdS+06DfoK7rA9zS\n23hVayuG9kQZ4je1lTCxECnnzYhdHfsyatAFXo/rSRgoWd1m71qVS0HQ6oWzqssm\naLxLUPjTf3nO/ZJ9M46nLA1ELwr7qjj3Uv+HVPk1btkLuIbW5w1YBkTbrQMdVIGm\nYMR2Pe7jsApZpgoV3YkNLtUl/Ph0FTMUvzeeKvMBfqhM1IkO4BrByql+XDkLTYOi\nQoRwlejcm5SFzI8SoQhBAXWVrdBCIlRmYJ9ROgRSPjH29PIUP/zIKbooOBDocmUR\ncmrDNbtxjqqc6sKZ9YPnVUQ5iTaxXaSCXsz4Jinj3V7Jf+GfzNbLEvfabehJcloI\nbfdQoTAZH53FEOwSPwWHigPOVUjsRUvj1czqhC6zcQdyDUdyQ6ZURqrQCmCpbLLw\n4pfBWAtQKj3IpNWiyQf0VPVDQBrHtQSHap7RoqP+pjFTPrroiVJlC3NqIHSwOGGU\neQeivxEeERZq4pzkEL1K\n=VwIZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T01:17:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKDI1N2UxZTA1NDM4YzIwMmM1Yzc5NzNjYmE4MDJlZmYyMWViNmFhMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa","sha":"b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa"}],"sha":"257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/257e1e05438c202c5c7973cba802eff21eb6aa36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:08Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:17:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): map script binaries to the package that installs them (#3222)\n\n## Summary\n\nA script binary now credits the package that installs it when the binary name and the package name are different. This removes false unused-dependency reports for `npm-run-all2` (through `run-p` and `run-s`), and for tools such as `ember-cli`, `@nestjs/cli`, `@capacitor/cli`, `@cucumber/cucumber`, `dependency-cruiser`, `commitizen`, `@typescript/native-preview`, `flow-bin`, `npm-check-updates`, `dotenv-cli`, `npm-package-json-lint`, `i18next-parser` and `@manypkg/cli` when `node_modules` is missing.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`resolve_binary_to_package` in `crates/core/src/scripts/resolve.rs` read a static binary table before `node_modules`. The table mapped `run-p` and `run-s` only to `npm-run-all`. Thus `npm-run-all2`, the maintained fork, got no credit, also with `node_modules` installed.\n\nThe table also had no entry for many binaries whose name is different from the package name. Without `node_modules`, the binary name stayed as the package name, and the declared package got no credit. A command-line tool in the tooling catalogue, or a plugin that needs a script reference (for example Ember), then reported its packages as unused.\n\n## Fix\n\n- A table entry now lists every package that can provide the binary. For example, `run-p` maps to `npm-run-all` and `npm-run-all2`.\n- `resolve_binary_to_packages` returns all candidates. When `node_modules` (the `.bin` link or the `bin` field) shows which candidate installs the binary, it returns only that package. An unrelated installed package does not override the table.\n- `resolve_known_dependency_binary` returns the first declared candidate.\n- The table has new entries for `ember`, `nest`, `cap`, `cucumber-js`, `depcruise` (and its sibling binaries), `cz`, `git-cz`, `tsgo`, `flow`, `ncu`, `dotenv`, `npmPkgJsonLint`, `i18next` and `manypkg`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New fixture `tests/fixtures/script-binary-package-credit` without `node_modules`. The integration test failed before the fix (all tools reported unused) and passes after it (only the control package is reported).\n- New unit tests cover the fork candidates, selection through the bin map and the `.bin` link, an unrelated installed package, and each new binary without `node_modules`.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core -p fallow-cli` pass.\n- Three real projects without these binaries in their scripts give the same `dead-code` JSON output before and after the change, except for the run ID.","tree":{"sha":"f312e7b84b24e03759d098ae4a03d410c176ac2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/f312e7b84b24e03759d098ae4a03d410c176ac2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa","verification":{"payload":"tree f312e7b84b24e03759d098ae4a03d410c176ac2b\nparent fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249428 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249428 +0200\n\nfix(deps): map script binaries to the package that installs them (#3222)\n\n## Summary\n\nA script binary now credits the package that installs it when the binary name and the package name are different. This removes false unused-dependency reports for `npm-run-all2` (through `run-p` and `run-s`), and for tools such as `ember-cli`, `@nestjs/cli`, `@capacitor/cli`, `@cucumber/cucumber`, `dependency-cruiser`, `commitizen`, `@typescript/native-preview`, `flow-bin`, `npm-check-updates`, `dotenv-cli`, `npm-package-json-lint`, `i18next-parser` and `@manypkg/cli` when `node_modules` is missing.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`resolve_binary_to_package` in `crates/core/src/scripts/resolve.rs` read a static binary table before `node_modules`. The table mapped `run-p` and `run-s` only to `npm-run-all`. Thus `npm-run-all2`, the maintained fork, got no credit, also with `node_modules` installed.\n\nThe table also had no entry for many binaries whose name is different from the package name. Without `node_modules`, the binary name stayed as the package name, and the declared package got no credit. A command-line tool in the tooling catalogue, or a plugin that needs a script reference (for example Ember), then reported its packages as unused.\n\n## Fix\n\n- A table entry now lists every package that can provide the binary. For example, `run-p` maps to `npm-run-all` and `npm-run-all2`.\n- `resolve_binary_to_packages` returns all candidates. When `node_modules` (the `.bin` link or the `bin` field) shows which candidate installs the binary, it returns only that package. An unrelated installed package does not override the table.\n- `resolve_known_dependency_binary` returns the first declared candidate.\n- The table has new entries for `ember`, `nest`, `cap`, `cucumber-js`, `depcruise` (and its sibling binaries), `cz`, `git-cz`, `tsgo`, `flow`, `ncu`, `dotenv`, `npmPkgJsonLint`, `i18next` and `manypkg`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New fixture `tests/fixtures/script-binary-package-credit` without `node_modules`. The integration test failed before the fix (all tools reported unused) and passes after it (only the control package is reported).\n- New unit tests cover the fork candidates, selection through the bin map and the `.bin` link, an unrelated installed package, and each new binary without `node_modules`.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core -p fallow-cli` pass.\n- Three real projects without these binaries in their scripts give the same `dead-code` JSON output before and after the change, except for the run ID.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEwUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+bcQAGZ/BA93rO/QM+tJA3S8ePCG\nuIUGafwXApH0+6oDF9wnKgmghIzTIrjHgXpP29VVn6Ewmsznr/W2t3TqB+EKVKU1\n7l1Z8LP43nuL9nUooWjMt2cl6z9wxQ1nP7xY/3LD0G/hAhwubks98rVrUbj5lhzd\nH1E4FN3NMlDn3CfIDQzpFsUfii/I12NOYe/G7nWDKa5CyrVqLOCiln7Wx7IuS8/i\n/uUmwlJgumrElwSnAovO6S8ZISdzGi9v75LDFIoJC0ry79ecW2NRtZO1SGjoJbuI\nv7N35Vd6qn7E1oTbVXyXNkdZB9+ZUzqR4l9FEwvmglM31HgwT3lsqcRDETO1wkd+\nDtBeOr8KAgyT9g0NA3o9CzfatdOUdHOYXsKelkt6Ui6Jl216nDTmhljYN1CDlfl6\n5QKy51XDGfWQ6a+fzJvc+GaHJd3GJa5qwfGtymihnNzYA/z12QR2cYmiLlYVbh/l\n9mTJfEXtIcLJimRv9FMi0PBu2D5zm718u24z9ycHHy2XjvXleYo6dtEvWpxYJt5D\n3omuSHEdPzW4+rhm9rkKpCtDHKN2K1k/a5yxuBK5umPJeUDz2Tq38Otuc9qDLyxF\nrC8zd6jRox8dpyZZvVDpA9XmgQG2D2Lx1kUUGZZVCaKCiz95/V6oWUvvNhhLPq7d\nE6uYTo/hcYENcxZCHQ6X\n=zDJt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T01:17:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa","node_id":"C_kwDORpPJVNoAKGI5ODc1ZjlkZjc4ZjFlMWFiNjVjZjZmNTQ0MTA3MTJmMDAwNTMxZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow/commit/fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8","sha":"fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8"}],"sha":"b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/b9875f9df78f1e1ab65cf6f54410712f000531fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:16:55Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:16:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(extract): follow JSDoc @import tags as type-only imports (#3221)\n\n## Summary\n\nA checked JavaScript file can load types with a JSDoc `@import` tag:\n\n```js\n/** @import { Config } from ''../types/config'' */\n/** @type {Config} */\nexport const config = { name: \"app\" };\n```\n\nBefore this change, fallow reported `types/config.d.ts` (or a plain `.ts` target) as an unused file and its types as unused. Now the tag keeps the target module used and credits the named types.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe JSDoc scanner in `crates/extract/src/parse.rs` read only `import(''./x'').Foo` type expressions. It had no parser for the `@import` tag, so no edge went to the target module. The gap also reached module declaration files: such a file is now an entry point only when something points to it, and the `@import` tag did not count.\n\n## Fix\n\n- A new scanner reads `@import` tags that start a JSDoc line. It records named and default bindings as type-only imports with no local binding, the same shape as the `import()` scanner. The clause can continue on the next lines until the module specifier or the next tag. A clause that does not parse adds no import.\n- A namespace binding (`@import * as ns from ''./mod''`) does not become a namespace import, because nothing narrows member access on a binding with no local name. A namespace import would then credit every export of the target module. Instead, the scanner reads the JSDoc type expressions of the same file for `ns.Member` and records a type-only named import for each member. A side-effect import keeps the target module reachable when the file uses no member. Prose outside a JSDoc type brace group gives no credit.\n- The extraction cache version changes, because cached modules from older versions do not hold these imports.\n- The CHANGELOG entry for orphan declaration files now names `entry` as the way to keep such a file and the modules that it imports. `ignorePatterns` and the `// fallow-ignore-file unused-file` comment only hide the report for the file.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New fixture `tests/fixtures/jsdoc-import-tag` with an integration test. It fails before the fix (four target files reported as unused) and passes after it.\n- Unit tests for named, aliased, quoted, default, mixed, empty and multi-line clauses, and for prose, `@imports` and broken clauses that must add no import. Two unit tests check that a namespace tag credits only the `ns.Member` references in JSDoc types.\n- The fixture has a namespace tag for `types/shapes.d.ts` and for `src/units.ts`. The unused type `Square` and the unused value `unusedScale` stay reported. With a namespace import, both were hidden.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-extract -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass. In the full CLI run, `saved_audit_reports_preserve_all_native_sections` failed once because a spawned process was not found. It passed when run again alone, and it does not touch JSDoc extraction.\n- Three real JavaScript and TypeScript projects without `@import` tags give the same `dead-code` JSON before and after the change.","tree":{"sha":"9297977ee2143fc12f00b0c04c19532151794518","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/9297977ee2143fc12f00b0c04c19532151794518"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8","verification":{"payload":"tree 9297977ee2143fc12f00b0c04c19532151794518\nparent 17e718f203c5e27fb695b8f8bfe6d1530dbc1b83\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249415 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249415 +0200\n\nfix(extract): follow JSDoc @import tags as type-only imports (#3221)\n\n## Summary\n\nA checked JavaScript file can load types with a JSDoc `@import` tag:\n\n```js\n/** @import { Config } from ''../types/config'' */\n/** @type {Config} */\nexport const config = { name: \"app\" };\n```\n\nBefore this change, fallow reported `types/config.d.ts` (or a plain `.ts` target) as an unused file and its types as unused. Now the tag keeps the target module used and credits the named types.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe JSDoc scanner in `crates/extract/src/parse.rs` read only `import(''./x'').Foo` type expressions. It had no parser for the `@import` tag, so no edge went to the target module. The gap also reached module declaration files: such a file is now an entry point only when something points to it, and the `@import` tag did not count.\n\n## Fix\n\n- A new scanner reads `@import` tags that start a JSDoc line. It records named and default bindings as type-only imports with no local binding, the same shape as the `import()` scanner. The clause can continue on the next lines until the module specifier or the next tag. A clause that does not parse adds no import.\n- A namespace binding (`@import * as ns from ''./mod''`) does not become a namespace import, because nothing narrows member access on a binding with no local name. A namespace import would then credit every export of the target module. Instead, the scanner reads the JSDoc type expressions of the same file for `ns.Member` and records a type-only named import for each member. A side-effect import keeps the target module reachable when the file uses no member. Prose outside a JSDoc type brace group gives no credit.\n- The extraction cache version changes, because cached modules from older versions do not hold these imports.\n- The CHANGELOG entry for orphan declaration files now names `entry` as the way to keep such a file and the modules that it imports. `ignorePatterns` and the `// fallow-ignore-file unused-file` comment only hide the report for the file.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New fixture `tests/fixtures/jsdoc-import-tag` with an integration test. It fails before the fix (four target files reported as unused) and passes after it.\n- Unit tests for named, aliased, quoted, default, mixed, empty and multi-line clauses, and for prose, `@imports` and broken clauses that must add no import. Two unit tests check that a namespace tag credits only the `ns.Member` references in JSDoc types.\n- The fixture has a namespace tag for `types/shapes.d.ts` and for `src/units.ts`. The unused type `Square` and the unused value `unusedScale` stay reported. With a namespace import, both were hidden.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-extract -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass. In the full CLI run, `saved_audit_reports_preserve_all_native_sections` failed once because a spawned process was not found. It passed when run again alone, and it does not touch JSDoc extraction.\n- Three real JavaScript and TypeScript projects without `@import` tags give the same `dead-code` JSON before and after the change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEwHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUS4QAA87gXsb73PRkNnLOw+9dAWv\nf9B7bIq1KgyeQcze03Dc1zyu0EPZl9FXESZDnKyRX4QNBje9TjnjNr7LHSM0e6DA\np1r8cl/Geoamr6ObODBRVWJ1FHp