/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/17e718f203c5e27fb695b8f8bfe6d1530dbc1b83"}],"sha":"fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/fa05efa57e2f12f19bc484f2c9ac6f9b3dc6afd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1352352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BartWaardenburg","id":1352352,"login":"BartWaardenburg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIzNTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BartWaardenburg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/commits/17e718f203c5e27fb695b8f8bfe6d1530dbc1b83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:16:41Z","email":"bart@waardenburg.dev","name":"Bart Waardenburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:16:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(plugins): credit the PostCSS plugins that postcss.config names (#3220)\n\n## Summary\n\nA Tailwind v4 project with the default Next.js shape reported `@tailwindcss/postcss` as an unused devDependency. The `postcss.config.mjs` of the project names that package. Other PostCSS plugins in the config, such as `autoprefixer`, had the same false positive.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe PostCSS plugin activated only on a declared `postcss` package. A bundler such as Next.js loads `postcss.config.*` with its own copy of PostCSS, so these projects often declare no `postcss` package. Thus fallow did not read the config, and the packages in its `plugins` object had no reference.\n\nTailwind v4 has no `tailwind.config.*` file. Since tooling credit needs evidence of use, the Tailwind plugin does not credit `@tailwindcss/postcss` in this shape, and the gap became visible.\n\n## Fix\n\nA `postcss.config.{ts,js,cjs,mjs}` file at the package root now also activates the PostCSS plugin. The plugin then reads the config and credits the packages that it names. A declared `postcss` package still activates the plugin as before.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New fixture `tests/fixtures/postcss-config-without-postcss-dependency` (Next.js app, Tailwind v4, no `postcss` package). The new integration test failed before the fix with `[\"@tailwindcss/postcss\", \"autoprefixer\"]` as unused devDependencies, and passes after the fix.\n- New unit test for the activation on the config file.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass.\n- On real projects with this shape, the false positive goes away and no other finding changes.","tree":{"sha":"e2a258f2230bea05f23907a4fb1ca7951e09bca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/trees/e2a258f2230bea05f23907a4fb1ca7951e09bca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fallow-rs/fallow/git/commits/17e718f203c5e27fb695b8f8bfe6d1530dbc1b83","verification":{"payload":"tree e2a258f2230bea05f23907a4fb1ca7951e09bca0\nparent f9dc240e4eb20873d6f0fb55f2d8b1dc58c7f795\nauthor Bart Waardenburg <bart@waardenburg.dev> 1791249401 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791249401 +0200\n\nfix(plugins): credit the PostCSS plugins that postcss.config names (#3220)\n\n## Summary\n\nA Tailwind v4 project with the default Next.js shape reported `@tailwindcss/postcss` as an unused devDependency. The `postcss.config.mjs` of the project names that package. Other PostCSS plugins in the config, such as `autoprefixer`, had the same false positive.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe PostCSS plugin activated only on a declared `postcss` package. A bundler such as Next.js loads `postcss.config.*` with its own copy of PostCSS, so these projects often declare no `postcss` package. Thus fallow did not read the config, and the packages in its `plugins` object had no reference.\n\nTailwind v4 has no `tailwind.config.*` file. Since tooling credit needs evidence of use, the Tailwind plugin does not credit `@tailwindcss/postcss` in this shape, and the gap became visible.\n\n## Fix\n\nA `postcss.config.{ts,js,cjs,mjs}` file at the package root now also activates the PostCSS plugin. The plugin then reads the config and credits the packages that it names. A declared `postcss` package still activates the plugin as before.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New fixture `tests/fixtures/postcss-config-without-postcss-dependency` (Next.js app, Tailwind v4, no `postcss` package). The new integration test failed before the fix with `[\"@tailwindcss/postcss\", \"autoprefixer\"]` as unused devDependencies, and passes after the fix.\n- New unit test for the activation on the config file.\n- `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy -p fallow-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p fallow-core` and `cargo test -p fallow-cli` pass.\n- On real projects with this shape, the false positive goes away and no other finding changes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEv5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATwwQAG9WlPnrMMdUXzJwNnxeH0hd\npe0l9tR1NtJRF6op23QfTGwkCIf4cAIaWbFp20Gh1wK0ZZmUpcH/jImD5sGGMQmi\nBCvEoQfO0N0yM4LE0+7UTZbm7tuknDh66LYnsznniaiTYXmTwRfCm10pWS2AoggI\nYZTcY8pR7C0waedSnjJyOjF9fAy9JSU5FRFlOLuXMUPrD4daTdBTgDsUTWsjUIgB\nI/Lt+7RMBCVW8ULQF26NgHAs62llcl2XTVdK9h0u+lyDz6G6EiE34c+iToiwwUG5\nIZUAwmL0C/XJCbzvYgblz107mbbWWQWWi5s2AB/ml9+aP45KnIXCltcuIWPX54U