ub/commit/76e5b13496456ec5450fd93823dca7c36e1cf813","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDc2ZTViMTM0OTY0NTZlYzU0NTBmZDkzODIzZGNhN2MzNmUxY2Y4MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08","sha":"0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08"}],"sha":"76e5b13496456ec5450fd93823dca7c36e1cf813","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/76e5b13496456ec5450fd93823dca7c36e1cf813"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-09T16:57:09Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-09T16:57:09Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Refine system architecture diagram: adjust module spacing and text positioning","tree":{"sha":"c5c6668b3451e9d6a30a9a4f893dcfa5230504c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/c5c6668b3451e9d6a30a9a4f893dcfa5230504c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDBhNTFlZTljZjhmODE5NTBhZmZmMzc3MzNkNWYxNTQ1MDU5OTZkMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e","sha":"700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e"}],"sha":"0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/0a51ee9cf8f81950afff37733d5f154505996d08"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:37:32Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:37:32Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 6: Cleanup - Delete role-module-config.ts + Document future enhancements\n\nDELETED:\n✗ role-module-config.ts - all functionality now in registry.json\n\nADDED:\n✓ docs/REGISTRY_FUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md - Design doc for potential improvements\n\nCurrent Implementation:\n✓ Single-domain assumption (all modules on localhost or same domain)\n✓ Complete remoteEntry URLs in registry\n✓ All module metadata centralized in registry.json\n✓ No hardcoded configurations anywhere\n✓ Build succeeds without role-module-config.ts\n✓ All 10 containers deployed and working\n\nFuture Enhancement Paths Documented:\n1. Multi-Domain Support - Deploy modules on different domains\n2. HTTPS Support - Protocol flexibility per module\n3. Authentication - Credentials for secured remotes\n4. Service Discovery - Dynamic module locations\n5. Environment-specific Registries - Different URLs per environment\n\nCOMPLETE: Registry-driven dynamic module loading implemented\n- Zero hardcoded module configurations\n- Built-in extensibility for future needs\n- Clean separation of concerns\n- Production-ready","tree":{"sha":"6ec7e4098a495768437eb54a24a1bd824d155a4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/6ec7e4098a495768437eb54a24a1bd824d155a4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDcwMGZiNjZkMDY0M2E3ZjY3ZmUwZTkxNjM3Yjg3MTRhZjQzYWJiMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37","sha":"578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37"}],"sha":"700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/700fb66d0643a7f67fe0e91637b8714af43abb0e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:22:28Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:22:28Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 4: Update ModuleDashboardComponent - use PluginRegistryService\n\nRefactored ModuleDashboardComponent to load modules from registry instead of\nhardcoded role-module-config.ts.\n\nRemoved:\n✗ Import of getModulesForRole() from role-module-config\n✗ Hardcoded ModuleConfig interface dependency\n✗ Static role-to-modules mappings\n\nAdded:\n✓ PluginRegistryService injection\n✓ Registry.loadRegistry() call in ngOnInit\n✓ Dynamic module loading via getAvailableModulesForRole(role)\n✓ AsyncModule initialization support\n\nKey changes:\n1. Import: Use PluginRegistryService and ModuleMetadata instead of role-module-config\n2. ModuleDisplay interface: Extends ModuleMetadata (from registry) instead of ModuleConfig\n3. Constructor: Inject PluginRegistryService\n4. ngOnInit:\n   - Now async function\n   - Load registry first\n   - Call loadModulesForRole(role)\n5. loadModulesForRole():\n   - Query registry.getAvailableModulesForRole(role)\n   - Map registry modules to ModuleDisplay with loading state\n\nResult:\n✓ Dashboard gets modules exclusively from registry\n✓ Role filtering from registry works\n✓ Can add/remove modules without touching component code\n✓ All 10 containers running and tested","tree":{"sha":"23e9aa337d985243cd05b0cced231c9e5446e4b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/23e9aa337d985243cd05b0cced231c9e5446e4b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDU3ODE4NGY1MmM2MjIyNjEwM2RjYmFiYWUyMDFiMTU2YTA3ZDhhMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9","sha":"4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9"}],"sha":"578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/578184f52c62226103dcbabae201b156a07d8a37"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:17:15Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:17:15Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 3: Refactor ModuleLoaderService - load configs from registry dynamically\n\nMajor refactoring: ModuleLoaderService now loads all module configurations from\nPluginRegistryService (registry.json) instead of hardcoded Maps.\n\nRemoved:\n✗ containerNames Map (6 hardcoded entries)\n✗ moduleConfigs Map (6 hardcoded module definitions)\n✗ All URL construction logic\n✗ Hardcoded port numbers and module references\n\nAdded:\n✓ PluginRegistryService injection\n✓ Registry loading on module load\n✓ Dynamic federation config retrieval via getModuleFederationConfig()\n✓ Registry-based module validation\n\nKey changes:\n1. Constructor: Inject PluginRegistryService\n2. loadModule():\n   - Load registry first\n   - Get federationConfig from registry.getModuleFederationConfig()\n   - Get containerName from registry module metadata\n   - Use registry values for remoteEntry, remoteName, exposedModule\n3. getAvailableModules(): Query registry.getAllEnabledModules()\n4. isModuleConfigured(): Check registry.getModuleByName()\n5. getVisibleModulesForRole(): Use registry.getAvailableModulesForRole()\n\nResult:\n✓ Single source of truth: registry.json\n✓ Zero hardcoded module configs\n✓ All 10 containers running and tested","tree":{"sha":"e8f7e295f9c25c2c27bdd3b5652dfa369f61b3cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/e8f7e295f9c25c2c27bdd3b5652dfa369f61b3cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDRhMzViZGY5NDdlZDgxNTQxMzRiMWNjMGZjNTQ5OTZhM2ZiZTU3Yzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf","sha":"5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf"}],"sha":"4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/4a35bdf947ed8154134b1cc0fc54996a3fbe57c9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:10:13Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:10:13Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 2: Update registry to store complete remoteEntry URLs\n\nChanged registry.json to store complete Federation URLs instead of ports:\n\nBefore:\n- Each module had ''port'' field (e.g., 4201)\n- Services had to construct http://localhost:PORT/remoteEntry.js\n\nAfter:\n- Each module has ''remoteEntry'' field with complete URL\n- Removed ''baseUrl'' - all URLs now explicit in registry\n- Services simply use registry values directly\n\nUpdated PluginRegistryService:\n- ModuleMetadata interface: replaced ''port'' with ''remoteEntry'' field\n- Simplified getModuleFederationConfig(): now returns registry values directly\n- Removed getRemoteEntryUrl(): no URL construction needed\n\nBenefits:\n✅ Registry is single source of truth for ALL federation config\n✅ No URL construction logic in code\n✅ Environment-independent - different registries for different environments\n✅ Simpler, more maintainable code\n✅ Easier to support different deployment architectures\n\nTested:\n✓ Shell app builds successfully\n✓ Registry container serving updated registry.json\n✓ All 10 containers running","tree":{"sha":"7c77c2dc5707e5d51dd9a2bfa5e709f058036d05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/7c77c2dc5707e5d51dd9a2bfa5e709f058036d05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDUwNDllOTkxM2FhYWU0Y2QwNzc1MzM1OTg5MDI0MjYyYjFlMTBhZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0","sha":"a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0"}],"sha":"5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/5049e9913aaae4cd0775335989024262b1e10adf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T20:53:34Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T20:53:34Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 2: Extend PluginRegistryService with module federation methods\n\nAdded federation-aware methods to PluginRegistryService:\n\n1. Extended ModuleMetadata interface:\n   - Added ''port'' field (e.g., 4201)\n   - Added ''remoteName'' field (e.g., ''demographicsApp'')\n   - Added ''exposedModule'' field (e.g., ''./DemographicsModule'')\n\n2. New methods for dynamic module loading:\n   - getModuleByName(name): Get module by display name\n   - getRemoteEntryUrl(moduleName): Build http://localhost:PORT/remoteEntry.js\n   - getModuleFederationConfig(moduleName): Get complete config for ModuleLoaderService\n\nThese methods enable ModuleLoaderService to load module configurations\nfrom registry instead of hardcoded Maps, supporting true dynamic loading.\n\nRegistry is now the single source of truth for:\n- Module availability and filtering\n- Module federation configuration (ports, remote names, exposed modules)\n- Role-based access control\n\nTested: Shell app builds and deploys successfully with new methods","tree":{"sha":"24580bc1a803ea5bd17db1db27336a3b8142a15d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/24580bc1a803ea5bd17db1db27336a3b8142a15d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKGE5YzA5ODZiODk0NTVmYTM2MzEyMzE0YzFhNWEzNDE5MWU1MjM4YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9","sha":"74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9"}],"sha":"a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/a9c0986b89455fa36312314c1a5a34191e5238b0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T20:21:09Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T20:21:09Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Fix: Enforce strict session timeout - reject refresh of expired tokens\n\nCRITICAL FIX: /auth/refresh endpoint now rejects expired tokens.\n\nPreviously:\n- Token expired after timeout\n- Any API call with expired token got 401\n- Interceptor called /auth/refresh with expired token\n- /auth/refresh accepted it (ignoreExpiration: true) and issued new one\n- User kept working indefinitely - timeout never actually happened\n\nNow:\n- Token expires after configured timeout (default: 60 minutes)\n- Any API call with expired token gets 401\n- Interceptor tries to refresh via /auth/refresh\n- /auth/refresh validates token is STILL VALID and rejects if expired\n- Interceptor catches 401 and logs user out, redirects to login\n- User returns to login page and must re-authenticate\n\nTested with 3-minute timeout:\n- User logs in and selects patient\n- After 3+ minutes, attempts action\n- Correctly redirected to login\n- Can re-authenticate and continue\n\nResult: True session timeout enforcement with clean UX","tree":{"sha":"013fc3d3680605247684a1bd1ca6e0d66a2253e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/013fc3d3680605247684a1bd1ca6e0d66a2253e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDc0ZGMwOTdkYWRmYmNhNWNiN2RlMjAwMTliODc4NDU3YWRiNTAwYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac","sha":"801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac"}],"sha":"74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/74dc097dadfbca5cb7de20019b878457adb500a9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T19:12:55Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T19:12:55Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Make session timeout granular to minutes for better testing flexibility\n\n- Change TOKEN_EXPIRATION_HOURS to TOKEN_EXPIRATION_MINUTES in backend/server.js\n- Default: 60 minutes (1 hour)\n- Can now be easily configured for testing (e.g., 3 minutes = TOKEN_EXPIRATION_MINUTES=3)\n- Updated docker-compose.yml environment variable","tree":{"sha":"8928e111b8be3f5397fd71898a5b318ddf1114d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/8928e111b8be3f5397fd71898a5b318ddf1114d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDgwMWU4MmZmNmNmOTJmOWM3YzMxMDRkNTcwNzc5OWE2M2E1MDZiYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5","sha":"d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5"}],"sha":"801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/801e82ff6cf92f9c7c3104d5707799a63a506bac"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T19:03:51Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T19:03:51Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Fix authentication session validation after service restart\n\n- Add /auth/validate endpoint to backend for token validation\n- Add validateTokenWithBackend() method to AuthService\n- Call token validation in dashboard.component.ts ngOnInit()\n- Redirect to login if token is invalid/expired\n- Session timeout remains 1 hour (configurable in next phase)\n- Resolves issue where stale tokens caused frozen UI after restarts","tree":{"sha":"015816b961664f6383a99bd982f87357511ee063","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/015816b961664f6383a99bd982f87357511ee063"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKGQ4NDQ5YzU5YjZmMDIzMTgwMDM4YzdlZjhhZjYyYzkzZWU4MmY0YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23","sha":"e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23"}],"sha":"d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/d8449c59b6f023180038c7ef8af62c93ee82f4c5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-02T18:29:28Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-02T18:29:28Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"feat(care-team): enhance seed data with varied provider pool and realistic variation\n\n- Rewrite seed-care-team.js with 30+ diverse healthcare providers across 12 specialty categories\n- Add helper functions for realistic data generation (generatePhone, generateEmail, generateStartDate)\n- Implement per-patient variation: 4-8 team members (increased from fixed count)\n- Random PCP selection from 4 primary care physicians\n- Diverse specialist assignments without replacement\n- Clear existing care team data before seeding for clean dataset\n- Add detailed console logging for team member assignments per patient\n- Result: Each patient now has unique, realistic care team composition","tree":{"sha":"8f5b0eac3b9f34be75bf213c6c09b236532317d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/8f5b0eac3b9f34be75bf213c6c09b236532317d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKGU4YjVkMDk1ZWJkODNjMGI4ZDE1NTM3N2MxM2VlOTI1YWJjZDZlMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/41d7eb9290c124eb1cc8fc719ea9c90a0264f53a","sha":"41d7eb9290c124eb1cc8fc719ea9c90a0264f53a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/41d7eb9290c124eb1cc8fc719ea9c90a0264f53a"}],"sha":"e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/e8b5d095ebd83c0b8d155377c13ee925abcd6e23"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/41d7eb9290c124eb1cc8fc719ea9c90a0264f53a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-27T22:22:59Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-27T22:22:59Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"docs: Add V3 mobile responsiveness implementation plan\n\n- Comprehensive m