","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-21T17:32:40Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 5e: Update comprehensive README documentation\n\n- Replaced outdated README with 537-line comprehensive guide\n- Added system architecture diagrams and micro-frontend design overview\n- Included authentication & session management technical details\n- Added quick start instructions for Docker and local development\n- Documented project structure and all module organization\n- Added API endpoint documentation with examples\n- Included troubleshooting guide and development workflows\n- Added roadmap for future phases\n- Updated with latest deployment information\n- Referenced Phase 5d session timeout implementation","tree":{"sha":"7d2c91879e7acb5bce9818c322b2e78227860198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/7d2c91879e7acb5bce9818c322b2e78227860198"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/567994b5a29912e1c19a96cb4d5db5b4d2d28572","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/567994b5a29912e1c19a96cb4d5db5b4d2d28572","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDU2Nzk5NGI1YTI5OTEyZTFjMTlhOTZjYjRkNWRiNWI0ZDJkMjg1NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188","sha":"25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188"}],"sha":"567994b5a29912e1c19a96cb4d5db5b4d2d28572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/567994b5a29912e1c19a96cb4d5db5b4d2d28572"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-21T17:24:41Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-21T17:24:41Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 5d: Implement Session Timeout & Token Refresh\n\n- Created TokenService for JWT decoding and expiration detection\n- Enhanced AuthService with refresh(), refreshIfNeeded(), hasValidToken() methods\n- Implemented token URL preservation for post-login redirect\n- Enhanced AuthGuard to check token validity and save return URLs\n- Updated all 4 JWT interceptors (shell, demographics, vitals, medications)\n  - Catch 401 responses and attempt silent token refresh\n  - Retry original request with new token if refresh succeeds\n  - Redirect to login with returnUrl if refresh fails\n  - Prevent infinite retry loops with hasRetried flag\n- Updated LoginComponent to handle returnUrl query param and session expiry banner\n- Applied authGuard to all protected routes in app.routes.ts\n- Updated Dockerfiles to install shared library dependencies\n- All modules compile successfully\n- All containers running and healthy on ports 4200-4205, 5001\n\nFeatures:\n✅ Silent token refresh (user unaware)\n✅ Graceful session timeout handling\n✅ User location preservation across auth redirects\n✅ Cross-module token synchronization\n✅ Automatic retry on 401 Unauthorized","tree":{"sha":"fe2359fc7b2938fd937d942bc133d587d16088a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/fe2359fc7b2938fd937d942bc133d587d16088a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDI1MTMxZTkxZWM0MzczYzc5ZTA3YWRjMjRiNDdhN2QzMTM4OGMxODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4","sha":"383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4"}],"sha":"25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/25131e91ec4373c79e07adc24b47a7d31388c188"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T22:49:27Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T22:49:27Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 5c: Implement Vitals Module\n\n- Created VitalsComponent with rxjs subscription management\n- Fetch vital signs from /api/patients/:id/vitals endpoint\n- 4-state template: loading spinner, error with retry, content with grid, empty state\n- Vital cards display: temperature, BP, heart rate, respiratory rate, O2 saturation\n- Helper methods for status classification and trend indicators (📈📉➡️)\n- History table showing last 10 vital readings with date/time\n- Responsive CSS with breakpoints for tablet (768px) and mobile (480px)\n- JWT interceptor for secure API calls\n- Test data created: 4 vital readings for patient 99999 (John Smith)\n- Module deployed on port 4202, serving remoteEntry.js","tree":{"sha":"bf5ea37bd5eaa9c106e9c66079f9955802f736f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/bf5ea37bd5eaa9c106e9c66079f9955802f736f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDM4MzY0OGMzZWM0MmU3OTZmYTViZjBjYzZiMTRmMjE0MGYyNzRiZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961","sha":"765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961"}],"sha":"383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/383648c3ec42e796fa5bf0cc6b14f2140f274bf4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T22:12:49Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T22:12:49Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 5b: Implement Medications module feature with patient medication display\n\n- Implement MedicationsComponent with patient medication data fetching from backend API\n- Add HTTP interceptor for JWT token injection in micro-frontend\n- Create comprehensive HTML template with 4 states: loading, error, success, empty\n- Add responsive CSS styling with mobile-first design and animations\n- Implement patient context retrieval from Shell app localStorage\n- Add helper methods for frequency labeling and date formatting\n- Update main-standalone.ts bootstrap configuration with interceptor support\n- Create JWT interceptor for medications module\n\nComponent Features:\n- Fetches medications from /api/patients/:id/medications endpoint\n- Displays medication cards with: name, dose, frequency, route, start date\n- Shows medication indication in highlighted blue section\n- Displays total medication count statistic\n- Handles loading state with spinner animation\n- Handles error state with retry functionality\n- Responsive design for mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports\n- Proper RxJS subscription cleanup with takeUntil pattern\n- Memory leak prevention with destroy$ subject pattern\n\nAll containers built and running successfully.\nMedications module accessible on port 4204.","tree":{"sha":"49062e81caa7d47a864d657e62660829e4473e52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/49062e81caa7d47a864d657e62660829e4473e52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDc2NWIzYmY3MGU3ZDE5MzE0N2RjZDJiNjQyOTY1YjQ5NzU4YWU5NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258","sha":"b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258"}],"sha":"765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/765b3bf70e7d193147dcd2b642965b49758ae961"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T21:48:49Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T21:48:49Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"Phase 5a: Implement Demographics module feature with full patient data display\n\n- Implement DemographicsComponent with patient data fetching from backend API\n- Add HTTP interceptor for JWT token injection in micro-frontend\n- Create comprehensive HTML template with 4 states: loading, error, success, empty\n- Add responsive CSS styling with mobile-first design and animations\n- Implement patient context retrieval from Shell app localStorage\n- Add helper methods for patient full name, age calculation, and date formatting\n- Clean up medications files from demographics module\n- Update TypeScript configuration for proper module paths\n- Fix main-standalone.ts bootstrap configuration\n\nComponent Features:\n- Fetches patient demographics from /api/patients/:id endpoint\n- Displays personal information: name, DOB, age, gender\n- Displays contact information: email (mailto), phone (tel) as clickable links\n- Handles loading state with spinner animation\n- Handles error state with retry functionality\n- Responsive design for mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports\n- Proper RxJS subscription cleanup with takeUntil pattern\n- Memory leak prevention with destroy$ subject pattern\n\nAll containers built and running successfully.","tree":{"sha":"547b7fc68584a63365e8459863f7947574743399","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/547b7fc68584a63365e8459863f7947574743399"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKGI4MmI0MmFhMGNjMThkNWJmNmExYzUxYzYyMGY2MjZkMjQxNDMyNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059","sha":"8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059"}],"sha":"b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/b82b42aa0cc18d5bf6a1c51c620f626d24143258"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T17:25:31Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T17:25:31Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"docs: Add Phase 5 Feature Implementation Roadmap\n\nCentral reference document for implementing features across all 5 modules.\n\nIncludes:\n- System architecture overview\n- Current skeleton status of all modules\n- Detailed Demographics implementation checklist (Phase 5a - First module)\n- Standard pattern template for all modules\n- Implementation sequence for remaining modules (Vitals, Labs, Medications, Visits)\n- Available API endpoints and sample data\n- Helper utilities and code snippets\n- Testing strategy\n- Progress tracking\n\nThis roadmap guides feature implementation starting with Demographics module,\nestablishing patterns that will be replicated across remaining 4 modules.\n\nDocumentation complete - ready to begin feature implementation.","tree":{"sha":"e95aea00277a4e52dc1ad3737d5062a1511592ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/trees/e95aea00277a4e52dc1ad3737d5062a1511592ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/git/commits/8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059","node_id":"C_kwDORpn-rNoAKDg4NjViZTBiMTYzODFlN2YwNmI5N2MzNTBlOGNkNmFhYmRmOWMwNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commit/c3c770971777d68b30c180b7f8b7f4152068d60b","sha":"c3c770971777d68b30c180b7f8b7f4152068d60b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/c3c770971777d68b30c180b7f8b7f4152068d60b"}],"sha":"8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/8865be0b16381e7f06b97c350e8cd6aabdf9c059"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jabbour-labs/patientrecords.pub/commits/c3c770971777d68b30c180b7f8b7f4152068d60b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T17:10:18Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T17:10:18Z","email":"dev@patientrecords.local","name":"Development Team"},"message":"feat: Add visits as module federation remote (port 4205) - Complete all 5 modules\n\n- Configured visits module as lazy-loaded remote on port 4205 (final module)\n- Visits module exposes VisitsModule via webpack module federation\n- Visits generates and serves remoteEntry.js for shell app consumption\n- Updated shell webpack.config.js with all five remotes (medications, demographics, vitals, labs, visits)\n- Updated shell app routes to lazy-load all five modules\n- Updated role-module-config.ts to include all five modules for all user roles\n- Created missing angular.json and tsconfig.app.json for visits module\n- Updated visits component to display ''Hi from the visits module'' message\n- Created styles.css for visits module\n- Fixed visits Dockerfile to use correct dist path\n\nAll services running successfully:\n- Shell app: port 4200 (5 module federation remotes configured)\n- Medications remote: port 4204 ✓\n- Demographics remote: port 4201 ✓\n- Vitals remote: port 4202 ✓\n- Labs remote: port 4203 ✓\n- Visits remote: port 4205 ✓\n- Backend API: port 5001 ✓\n- MongoDB: port 27017 ✓\n\nDashboard displays all five module tabs:\n1. Demographics\n2. Vitals\n3. Labs\n4. Visi